{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.16","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"colab":{"provenance":[]},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/arbazdevhive/rag-retrieval-benchmark?scriptVersionId=365164101\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"id":"cell-001","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Biomedical RAG Benchmark: Chunking, Hybrid Retrieval, Reranking, and Evidence-Bounded Generation\n\nThis notebook implements a reproducible end-to-end benchmark on the **BEIR NFCorpus test split**. It evaluates the full factorial retrieval design (3 chunkers × 3 first-stage retrieval methods × 2 reranking conditions = 18 configurations), then runs three pre-specified RAG generation conditions on one shared sample of 100 test queries.\n\n**Runtime:** Kaggle Notebook with Internet enabled and a GPU accelerator (one or two NVIDIA T4 GPUs are supported). Execute every cell from top to bottom. The notebook creates `RAG_Benchmark_Results/` and, only after its automated checks pass, `RAG_Benchmark_Results.zip`.\n\n**Scientific safeguards:** the dense bi-encoder is fine-tuned only on train qrels, selected on dev qrels, and evaluated on a held-out test split; immutable base-model revisions are verified before use; all retrieval metrics use the same 323 test queries and parent-document relevance judgments; generated answers are actual model outputs; invalid outputs remain failures; NLI and similarity scores are explicitly treated as proxies rather than clinical correctness.\n\n**Relationship to the supplied manuscript:** the experiment follows its NFCorpus test-set scope, three chunking strategies, BM25/dense/RRF retrieval, cross-encoder reranking, parent-document aggregation, and paired evaluation. The manuscript states that its historical run did not retain model revision hashes and produced 300 empty generation outputs. This notebook does not assign new hashes to that historical run or reuse its empty outputs. It defines a fresh, pinned rerun and records its own provenance.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-001b","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Revision note (v23) — changes relative to the previous run\n\nThe previous run (fingerprint `1f51c230…`) produced 289/300 valid answers; 11 final outputs were invalid and the archive step failed. Inspection of `generation_attempts.csv` showed three causes, all fixed here:\n\n1. **Prompt leakage.** The old instruction named the phrase *“Evidence-grounded answer”* in a prohibition; FLAN-T5 copied it (`Evidence-grounded`, `Diet and Cellulite Evidence-grounded`). The instruction is now purely positive (no forbidden strings quoted).\n2. **Title-style queries echoed.** Queries such as *“Does Cholesterol Size Matter?”* or *“Dr. Dean Ornish”* were repeated verbatim. Answers now end with an explicit “write one or two complete sentences” cue, and up to **two** same-evidence recovery attempts are allowed (plain restatement, then a question–answer form).\n3. **Validation design.** A 100% validity gate hid the real result. The hard gate is now *no empty/failed outputs*; the completion rate is **reported** per condition. The notebook-file check no longer blocks the ZIP.\n\n**Disclosure for the manuscript:** these prompt revisions were made after observing failures on the same 100-query generation sample. Retrieval metrics, the test qrels used for scoring, and model pins are unchanged; state this explicitly in the Methods.\n","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-002","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Study background and official sources\n\nThe supplied manuscript motivates a controlled comparison of chunking, first-stage retrieval, and reranking. Its reported dataset audit specifies 3,633 NFCorpus documents, 323 test queries, and 12,334 document-level relevance judgments. Its evaluation convention uses graded nDCG, Recall@K, MRR@10, Precision@10, and truncated MAP@10 normalized by `min(number_of_relevant_documents, K)`. This notebook reproduces those definitions and reports latency boundaries explicitly.\n\nThe sources below were consulted before implementation. They are primary project documentation, official model cards, or the original RRF publication:\n\n1. [BEIR repository and dataset catalogue](https://github.com/beir-cellar/beir) — benchmark loader, dataset split conventions, NFCorpus metadata and checksum; official archive qrels include train, dev, and test partitions.\n2. [BEIR NFCorpus dataset card](https://huggingface.co/datasets/BeIR/nfcorpus) — corpus and query split metadata.\n3. [Official BEIR NFCorpus archive](https://public.ukp.informatik.tu-darmstadt.de/thakur/BEIR/datasets/nfcorpus.zip) — source archive downloaded by this notebook.\n4. [all-MiniLM-L6-v2 model card](https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2) and [pinned commit](https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2/tree/1110a243fdf4706b3f48f1d95db1a4f5529b4d41) — 384-dimensional sentence embeddings; the model card documents its default sequence truncation behavior.\n5. [MS MARCO MiniLM cross-encoder model card](https://huggingface.co/cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L6-v2) and [pinned commit](https://huggingface.co/cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L6-v2/tree/233902d25c440f23af6f7d6e94d2946bac0bee0a) — pairwise passage reranking.\n6. [FLAN-T5-large model card](https://huggingface.co/google/flan-t5-large) and [pinned commit](https://huggingface.co/google/flan-t5-large/tree/0613663d0d48ea86ba8cb3d7a44f0f65dc596a2a) — instruction-following sequence-to-sequence generation.\n7. [DeBERTa-v3 NLI cross-encoder model card](https://huggingface.co/cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-base) and [pinned commit](https://huggingface.co/cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-base/tree/6c749ce3425cd33b46d187e45b92bbf96ee12ec7) — three-way contradiction/entailment/neutral inference.\n8. [Sentence Transformers embedding documentation](https://www.sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/usage/semantic_textual_similarity.html), [training loss documentation](https://www.sbert.net/docs/package_reference/sentence_transformer/losses.html), and [CrossEncoder usage documentation](https://www.sbert.net/docs/cross_encoder/usage/usage.html) — normalized embeddings, in-batch contrastive training concepts, and second-stage pairwise scoring.\n9. [Official NFCorpus qrels dataset repository](https://huggingface.co/datasets/BeIR/nfcorpus-qrels) — separate train, development, and test TSV relevance-judgment files.\n10. [Hugging Face Transformers generation documentation](https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main_classes/text_generation) — explicit `max_new_tokens`, `min_new_tokens`, decoding strategy, and generation-score interfaces.\n11. [The Probabilistic Relevance Framework: BM25 and Beyond](https://doi.org/10.1561/1500000019) — primary methodological reference for BM25.\n12. [Original Reciprocal Rank Fusion paper](https://doi.org/10.1145/1571941.1572114) — rank-only fusion of independently produced rankings.\n13. [SummaC: Re-Visiting NLI-based Models for Inconsistency Detection in Summarization](https://aclanthology.org/2022.tacl-1.10/) — methodological background for using entailment-style NLI as a text-consistency proxy.\n14. [rank_bm25 implementation](https://github.com/dorianbrown/rank_bm25) — Okapi BM25 implementation used for lexical retrieval.\n\nThe four model SHAs below are **new, explicit pins for this rerun**. They are not represented as revisions used by the historical experiment. Every SHA is checked against the Hugging Face Hub before downloading weights.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-003","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Runtime and dependencies\n\nLarge ML packages are not upgraded automatically. The notebook installs only missing dependencies and records the versions actually used. It does not require an API key, external inference service, hidden local dataset, or proprietary checkpoint.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-004","cell_type":"code","source":"import os, sys, platform, json, time, math, random, re, csv, hashlib, shutil, zipfile, urllib.request, subprocess, importlib, importlib.metadata as importlib_metadata, warnings, gc, datetime, textwrap\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom collections import Counter, defaultdict\nwarnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\", category=FutureWarning)\n\n# Install only missing packages. Kaggle's preinstalled PyTorch/CUDA stack is retained.\nPACKAGE_REQUIREMENTS = {\n    \"numpy\": \"numpy\", \"pandas\": \"pandas\", \"matplotlib\": \"matplotlib\", \"scipy\": \"scipy\",\n    \"torch\": None, \"transformers\": \"transformers\", \"sentence_transformers\": \"sentence-transformers\",\n    \"huggingface_hub\": \"huggingface_hub\", \"rank_bm25\": \"rank-bm25==0.2.2\", \"tqdm\": \"tqdm\", \"psutil\": \"psutil\",\n    \"sentencepiece\": \"sentencepiece\", \"google.protobuf\": \"protobuf\", \"tabulate\": \"tabulate\",\n    \"cycler\": \"cycler\", \"PIL\": \"pillow\"\n}\nfor module_name, pip_name in PACKAGE_REQUIREMENTS.items():\n    try:\n        importlib.import_module(module_name)\n    except Exception:\n        if pip_name is None:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Required runtime package {module_name!r} is missing; use a Kaggle GPU notebook runtime.\")\n        result = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"pip\", \"install\", \"-q\", \"--disable-pip-version-check\", pip_name], capture_output=True, text=True)\n        if result.returncode != 0:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Could not install {pip_name}: {result.stderr[-2000:]}\")\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nimport torch\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use(\"Agg\")\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom cycler import cycler\n# Okabe-Ito-inspired colorblind-friendly cycle for all generated figures.\nplt.rcParams[\"axes.prop_cycle\"] = cycler(color=[\"#0072B2\", \"#E69F00\", \"#009E73\", \"#56B4E9\", \"#D55E00\", \"#CC79A7\", \"#F0E442\", \"#000000\"])\nplt.rcParams[\"figure.dpi\"] = 120\nfrom scipy import stats as scipy_stats\nfrom tqdm.auto import tqdm\nfrom IPython.display import display\n\nIN_KAGGLE = Path(\"/kaggle\").exists()\nprint(\"Python:\", sys.version.split()[0])\nprint(\"Platform:\", platform.platform())\nprint(\"PyTorch:\", torch.__version__, \"| CUDA:\", torch.version.cuda, \"| GPU count:\", torch.cuda.device_count())\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    for i in range(torch.cuda.device_count()):\n        print(f\"GPU {i}: {torch.cuda.get_device_name(i)} | {torch.cuda.get_device_properties(i).total_memory / 1e9:.1f} GB\")\nelse:\n    print(\"WARNING: no CUDA GPU detected. CPU fallback is technically supported but may be very slow.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:52:39.52082Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:52:39.521141Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:53:35.697531Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T06:52:39.521118Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:53:35.69682Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Python: 3.13.16\nPlatform: Linux-6.18.55+-x86_64-with-glibc2.39\nPyTorch: 2.11.0+cu130 | CUDA: 13.0 | GPU count: 2\nGPU 0: Tesla T4 | 15.6 GB\nGPU 1: Tesla T4 | 15.6 GB\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"id":"cell-005","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Deterministic setup and experiment configuration\n\nThe test split is used only for evaluation. One seeded sample of 100 test queries is shared across all generation conditions. The retrieval sweep evaluates every available test query in every configuration. Retrieval and generation parameters are declared before any model outputs are produced.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-006","cell_type":"code","source":"SEED = 20261023\nos.environ.setdefault(\"CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG\", \":4096:8\")\nos.environ.setdefault(\"TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM\", \"false\")\nrandom.seed(SEED)\nnp.random.seed(SEED)\ntorch.manual_seed(SEED)\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\ntorch.backends.cudnn.deterministic = True\ntorch.backends.cudnn.benchmark = False\ntry:\n    torch.use_deterministic_algorithms(True, warn_only=True)\nexcept Exception as exc:\n    print(\"Deterministic-algorithm setting warning:\", repr(exc))\n\nOUT = Path(\"/kaggle/working/RAG_Benchmark_Results\") if IN_KAGGLE else (Path.cwd() / \"RAG_Benchmark_Results\")\nRES = OUT / \"results\"\nFIG = OUT / \"figures\"\nREP = OUT / \"reports\"\nCKPT = OUT / \"checkpoints\"\nCACHE = OUT / \"cache\"\nfor folder in (OUT, RES, FIG, REP, CKPT, CACHE):\n    folder.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\nRUN_STARTED_UTC = datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\")\n\nMODEL_SPECS = {\n    \"embedding\": {\"repo_id\": \"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\", \"revision\": \"1110a243fdf4706b3f48f1d95db1a4f5529b4d41\"},\n    \"reranker\": {\"repo_id\": \"cross-encoder/ms-marco-MiniLM-L6-v2\", \"revision\": \"233902d25c440f23af6f7d6e94d2946bac0bee0a\"},\n    \"generator\": {\"repo_id\": \"google/flan-t5-large\", \"revision\": \"0613663d0d48ea86ba8cb3d7a44f0f65dc596a2a\"},\n    \"nli\": {\"repo_id\": \"cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-base\", \"revision\": \"6c749ce3425cd33b46d187e45b92bbf96ee12ec7\"},\n}\n\nCFG = {\n    \"seed\": SEED,\n    \"dataset\": {\n        \"name\": \"BEIR NFCorpus\", \"split\": \"test\",\n        \"url\": \"https://public.ukp.informatik.tu-darmstadt.de/thakur/BEIR/datasets/nfcorpus.zip\",\n        \"expected_md5\": \"a89dba18a62ef92f7d323ec890a0d38d\",\n        \"expected\": {\"documents\": 3633, \"queries\": 323, \"qrels\": 12334},\n    },\n    \"chunking\": [\n        {\"name\": \"fixed_128\", \"kind\": \"fixed\", \"target\": 128, \"overlap\": 0},\n        {\"name\": \"fixed_256_overlap32\", \"kind\": \"fixed\", \"target\": 256, \"overlap\": 32},\n        {\"name\": \"sentence_bounded_256\", \"kind\": \"sentence\", \"target\": 256, \"overlap\": 0},\n    ],\n    \"max_chunk_tokens\": 384,\n    \"candidate_depth\": 100,\n    \"rerank_depth\": 20,\n    \"rerank_chunks_per_document\": 3,\n    \"rrf_k\": 60,\n    \"cutoffs\": [1, 5, 10],\n    \"retrieval\": {\"dense_batch_size\": 128, \"reranker_batch_size\": 64, \"cross_encoder_max_length\": 512},\n    \"training\": {\n        \"component\": \"dense bi-encoder\", \"epochs\": 3, \"batch_size\": 32,\n        \"learning_rate\": 2e-5, \"weight_decay\": 0.01, \"temperature\": 0.05,\n        \"max_grad_norm\": 1.0, \"validation_chunking\": \"fixed_256_overlap32\",\n        \"selection_metric\": \"development nDCG@10\",\n        \"loss\": \"in-batch contrastive cross-entropy with one positive document per training query\",\n    },\n    \"generation\": {\n        \"n_queries\": 100, \"top_passages\": 5, \"max_new_tokens\": 128, \"min_new_tokens\": 8,\n        \"do_sample\": False, \"num_beams\": 4, \"num_return_sequences\": 1,\n        \"early_stopping\": True, \"length_penalty\": 1.0,\n        \"no_repeat_ngram_size\": 3, \"repetition_penalty\": 1.08,\n        \"precision\": \"FP32\",\n        \"min_answer_words\": 5,\n        \"prompt_instruction\": \"You are a biomedical literature evidence synthesizer. Use only facts explicitly supported by the supplied excerpts. The information need may be a question, a short topic phrase, a condition, or a person name. If the excerpts directly contain a finding about it, report that finding in one or two complete factual sentences (what was found, and in which population or study model when the excerpt says so). Add no facts from memory. If no excerpt directly supports a finding, answer exactly: The retrieved excerpts do not provide enough information to answer this topic. Always write full sentences with a subject and a verb. Do not claim clinical certainty.\",\n        \"recovery_instruction\": \"Read the source excerpts and write one or two complete sentences stating what they report about the topic. Use only the excerpts. If they contain no direct finding, answer exactly: The retrieved excerpts do not provide enough information to answer this topic.\",\n        \"recovery_instruction_2\": \"Answer the question using only the source excerpts, in one complete sentence. If the excerpts contain no direct finding, answer exactly: The retrieved excerpts do not provide enough information to answer this topic.\",\n        \"max_recovery_attempts\": 2,\n    },\n    \"nli\": {\"threshold\": 0.50, \"max_passages_per_claim\": 5, \"max_claims_per_answer\": 8, \"min_claim_words\": 4, \"max_length\": 512},\n    \"bootstrap\": {\"n_resamples\": 10000, \"alpha\": 0.05},\n}\nGEN_CONDITIONS = [\n    {\"id\": \"C1_fixed128_bm25\", \"chunking\": \"fixed_128\", \"retrieval\": \"bm25\", \"rerank\": False},\n    {\"id\": \"C2_fixed256o32_hybrid\", \"chunking\": \"fixed_256_overlap32\", \"retrieval\": \"hybrid\", \"rerank\": False},\n    {\"id\": \"C3_fixed256o32_hybrid_rerank\", \"chunking\": \"fixed_256_overlap32\", \"retrieval\": \"hybrid\", \"rerank\": True},\n]\n\n# Machine-readable pre-run configuration. No measured results are placed here.\n(RES / \"config.json\").write_text(json.dumps(CFG | {\"models\": MODEL_SPECS, \"generation_conditions\": GEN_CONDITIONS}, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(\"Output:\", OUT)\nprint(\"Retrieval grid:\", len(CFG[\"chunking\"]) * 3 * 2, \"configurations\")\nprint(\"Generation conditions:\", [c[\"id\"] for c in GEN_CONDITIONS])","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:53:35.699929Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:53:35.700622Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:53:35.737556Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T06:53:35.700547Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:53:35.736877Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Output: /kaggle/working/RAG_Benchmark_Results\nRetrieval grid: 18 configurations\nGeneration conditions: ['C1_fixed128_bm25', 'C2_fixed256o32_hybrid', 'C3_fixed256o32_hybrid_rerank']\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"id":"cell-007","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Model provenance and immutable checkpoint resolution\n\nThe new run pins four public models: a general-purpose sentence encoder, an MS MARCO passage reranker, FLAN-T5-large, and an NLI cross-encoder. The sentence encoder is not claimed to be biomedical-specialized. Revisions are checked by full 40-character commit SHA and downloaded as local snapshots. Model identifiers and SHAs are new-run provenance only; the supplied manuscript explicitly says the historical run did not retain resolved revisions.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-008","cell_type":"code","source":"from huggingface_hub import HfApi, snapshot_download\nHF_API = HfApi()\nSHA_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"^[0-9a-f]{40}$\")\nMODEL_PATHS = {}\nMODEL_REVISIONS = {}\nMODEL_ALLOW_PATTERNS = [\"*.json\", \"*.txt\", \"*.model\", \"1_Pooling/*\"]  # Weight files are selected per repository below.\nMODEL_IGNORE_PATTERNS = [\"*.onnx\", \"*.h5\", \"*.msgpack\", \"*.ot\", \"flax_model.*\", \"tf_model.*\", \"openvino*\", \"onnx/*\", \"rust_model.ot\"]\n\ndef sha256_file(path, block_size=1024 * 1024):\n    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n    with open(path, \"rb\") as stream:\n        for block in iter(lambda: stream.read(block_size), b\"\"):\n            digest.update(block)\n    return digest.hexdigest()\n\ndef save_json(path, obj):\n    path = Path(path)\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    temp = path.with_suffix(path.suffix + \".tmp\")\n    temp.write_text(json.dumps(obj, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False, default=str), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    os.replace(temp, path)\n\ndef resolve_model(role, spec):\n    repo_id, revision = spec[\"repo_id\"], spec[\"revision\"]\n    if not SHA_PATTERN.fullmatch(revision):\n        raise ValueError(f\"Invalid immutable SHA for {role}: {revision}\")\n    info = HF_API.model_info(repo_id, revision=revision, files_metadata=True)\n    if info.sha != revision:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Hub revision mismatch for {repo_id}: requested {revision}, received {info.sha}\")\n    hub_files = [item.rfilename for item in (info.siblings or [])]\n    safe_weight_files = [name for name in hub_files if name.endswith(\".safetensors\")]\n    bin_weight_files = [name for name in hub_files if name.endswith(\".bin\")]\n    # Download one PyTorch-compatible weight format only. This avoids doubling disk use.\n    selected_weight_files = safe_weight_files if safe_weight_files else bin_weight_files\n    if not selected_weight_files:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"No safetensors or PyTorch bin weights exist for {repo_id}@{revision}\")\n    allow_patterns = [\"*.json\", \"*.txt\", \"*.model\", \"1_Pooling/*\"] + selected_weight_files\n    local_dir = snapshot_download(\n        repo_id=repo_id, revision=revision,\n        allow_patterns=allow_patterns,\n        ignore_patterns=MODEL_IGNORE_PATTERNS,\n    )\n    local_path = Path(local_dir)\n    if local_path.name != revision:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Downloaded snapshot path does not identify immutable revision: {local_path}\")\n    weight_files = [name for name in selected_weight_files if (local_path / name).is_file()]\n    if not weight_files:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Selected PyTorch checkpoint weights were not downloaded for {repo_id}@{revision}\")\n    local_hashes = {name: sha256_file(local_path / name) for name in weight_files}\n    sibling_map = {item.rfilename: item for item in (info.siblings or [])}\n    remote_hashes = {}\n    for name in weight_files:\n        lfs = getattr(sibling_map.get(name), \"lfs\", None)\n        remote_hash = getattr(lfs, \"sha256\", None) if lfs is not None else None\n        remote_hashes[name] = remote_hash\n        if remote_hash and remote_hash != local_hashes[name]:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Weight hash mismatch for {repo_id}/{name}\")\n    from transformers import AutoConfig\n    config = AutoConfig.from_pretrained(str(local_path), local_files_only=True)\n    record = {\n        \"role\": role, \"repo_id\": repo_id, \"requested_commit_sha\": revision,\n        \"resolved_commit_sha\": info.sha, \"snapshot_path\": str(local_path),\n        \"weight_files\": weight_files, \"local_weight_sha256\": local_hashes,\n        \"hub_weight_sha256_when_available\": remote_hashes,\n        \"config_architectures\": getattr(config, \"architectures\", None),\n        \"model_type\": getattr(config, \"model_type\", None),\n        \"verified_at_utc\": datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(timespec=\"seconds\"),\n        \"loading_status\": \"revision_verified_and_snapshot_downloaded\",\n    }\n    MODEL_PATHS[role] = str(local_path)\n    MODEL_REVISIONS[role] = record\n    return record\n\nfor role, spec in MODEL_SPECS.items():\n    rec = resolve_model(role, spec)\n    print(f\"{role:10s} {rec['repo_id']} @ {rec['resolved_commit_sha']}\")\n\nassert set(MODEL_REVISIONS) == set(MODEL_SPECS)\nREV_TABLE = pd.DataFrame([\n    {\"role\": r[\"role\"], \"repository\": r[\"repo_id\"], \"commit_sha\": r[\"resolved_commit_sha\"],\n     \"weight_files\": \";\".join(r[\"weight_files\"]), \"loading_status\": r[\"loading_status\"]}\n    for r in MODEL_REVISIONS.values()\n])\ndisplay(REV_TABLE)\nsave_json(RES / \"model_revisions.json\", {\n    \"note\": \"These SHAs are explicit pins for this new rerun; they are not retrospective revisions for the historical manuscript experiment.\",\n    \"models\": MODEL_REVISIONS,\n})","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:53:35.73873Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:53:35.739064Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:54:17.884898Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T