   <td>6734</td>\n      <td>3633</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>1.854</td>\n      <td>195.501</td>\n      <td>237.0</td>\n      <td>256.0</td>\n      <td>256</td>\n      <td>5.332</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>2</th>\n      <td>sentence_bounded_256</td>\n      <td>256</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>6751</td>\n      <td>3633</td>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>1.858</td>\n      <td>180.310</td>\n      <td>208.0</td>\n      <td>253.0</td>\n      <td>384</td>\n      <td>25.317</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":6},{"id":"cell-015","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 8. Training or fine-tuning protocol\n\nA real dense bi-encoder fine-tuning stage is performed using only NFCorpus `train` qrels. One positively judged document is selected per training query with a fixed seed; an in-batch contrastive cross-entropy objective treats the paired document as the positive and other batch documents as negatives. Checkpoint selection uses exact document-level nDCG@10 on the separate `dev` qrels after retrieval over the fixed-256/32-overlap chunk index. The test qrels are not visible to the optimizer or checkpoint-selection function. The reranker, generator, and NLI evaluator remain pretrained and pinned. This is fine-tuning, not pretraining from scratch.\n\nThe in-batch objective can treat an unlabelled relevant document for another query as a negative when qrels are incomplete. The number of selected pairs, positive-document collisions, per-epoch training loss, development nDCG@10, best epoch, and local checkpoint hashes are saved. The baseline encoder is evaluated on `dev` before training; the best checkpoint is selected from baseline plus completed epochs, so a non-improving fine-tune is not falsely described as an improvement.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-016","cell_type":"code","source":"import torch.nn.functional as F\n\nTRAINING_CFG = CFG[\"training\"]\nTRAIN_DEVICE = \"cuda:0\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\nTRAIN_RNG = random.Random(SEED + 31)\n\n# One deterministic positive per training query. No validation or test query/qrel enters this pair list.\nTRAIN_PAIRS = []\ntrain_positive_doc_ids = []\ntrain_skipped_qids = []\nused_positive_docs = set()\nfor qid in sorted(TRAIN_QRELS):\n    positive_ids = [did for did, grade in TRAIN_QRELS[qid].items() if grade > 0 and did in CORPUS and CORPUS[did][\"text\"].strip()]\n    if not positive_ids or not ALL_QUERIES.get(qid, \"\").strip():\n        train_skipped_qids.append(qid)\n        continue\n    shuffled = positive_ids.copy()\n    TRAIN_RNG.shuffle(shuffled)\n    unused = [did for did in shuffled if did not in used_positive_docs]\n    chosen_doc = unused[0] if unused else shuffled[0]\n    used_positive_docs.add(chosen_doc)\n    train_positive_doc_ids.append(chosen_doc)\n    TRAIN_PAIRS.append({\"query_id\": qid, \"doc_id\": chosen_doc, \"query\": ALL_QUERIES[qid], \"document\": CORPUS[chosen_doc][\"text\"]})\n\nif len(TRAIN_PAIRS) < TRAINING_CFG[\"batch_size\"]:\n    raise RuntimeError(f\"Only {len(TRAIN_PAIRS)} valid training pairs; cannot run the configured in-batch contrastive training.\")\n\nDEV_QUERY_IDS = sorted(qid for qid, rels in DEV_QRELS.items() if any(g > 0 for g in rels.values()))\nif not DEV_QUERY_IDS:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"NFCorpus development qrels contain no positive queries; checkpoint selection cannot proceed.\")\n\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nTRAIN_MODEL = SentenceTransformer(MODEL_PATHS[\"embedding\"], device=TRAIN_DEVICE)\ntrain_encoder_config = AutoConfig.from_pretrained(MODEL_PATHS[\"embedding\"], local_files_only=True)\nTRAIN_MODEL.max_seq_length = min(386, int(getattr(train_encoder_config, \"max_position_embeddings\", 512)))\nTRAIN_MODEL.to(TRAIN_DEVICE)\n\nTRAIN_CHUNKS = CHUNKS[TRAINING_CFG[\"validation_chunking\"]]\nDEV_CHUNK_TEXTS = [c[\"text\"] for c in TRAIN_CHUNKS]\nDEV_CHUNK_DOC_IDS = [c[\"parent_doc_id\"] for c in TRAIN_CHUNKS]\nDEV_DOC_IDS_BY_CHUNK = np.asarray(DEV_CHUNK_DOC_IDS, dtype=object)\n\ndef compute_dev_ndcg10(model):\n    model.eval()\n    with torch.no_grad():\n        doc_vectors = model.encode(\n            DEV_CHUNK_TEXTS, batch_size=CFG[\"retrieval\"][\"dense_batch_size\"],\n            convert_to_numpy=True, normalize_embeddings=True, show_progress_bar=True,\n        ).astype(np.float32)\n        dev_qtexts = [ALL_QUERIES[qid] for qid in DEV_QUERY_IDS]\n        query_vectors = model.encode(\n            dev_qtexts, batch_size=CFG[\"retrieval\"][\"dense_batch_size\"],\n            convert_to_numpy=True, normalize_embeddings=True, show_progress_bar=False,\n        ).astype(np.float32)\n    if not np.isfinite(doc_vectors).all() or not np.isfinite(query_vectors).all():\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Non-finite vectors during development checkpoint selection\")\n    per_query = []\n    for qid, qvec in zip(DEV_QUERY_IDS, query_vectors):\n        scores = doc_vectors @ qvec\n        order = np.argsort(-scores, kind=\"stable\")\n        best_doc_score = {}\n        for index in order:\n            did = str(DEV_DOC_IDS_BY_CHUNK[int(index)])\n            score = float(scores[int(index)])\n            if did not in best_doc_score or score > best_doc_score[did]:\n                best_doc_score[did] = score\n        ranked = [did for did, _ in sorted(best_doc_score.items(), key=lambda item: (-item[1], item[0]))[:10]]\n        relevant = {did: float(grade) for did, grade in DEV_QRELS[qid].items() if grade > 0}\n        dcg = sum((2.0 ** relevant.get(did, 0.0) - 1.0) / math.log2(rank + 1) for rank, did in enumerate(ranked, start=1))\n        ideal = sorted(relevant.values(), reverse=True)[:10]\n        idcg = sum((2.0 ** grade - 1.0) / math.log2(rank + 1) for rank, grade in enumerate(ideal, start=1))\n        per_query.append(dcg / idcg if idcg > 0 else np.nan)\n    values = np.asarray(per_query, dtype=float)\n    if not np.isfinite(values).all():\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Development nDCG@10 contains non-finite values\")\n    return float(values.mean())\n\nBEST_ENCODER_DIR = CKPT / \"dense_encoder_selected\"\nif BEST_ENCODER_DIR.exists():\n    shutil.rmtree(BEST_ENCODER_DIR)\nBEST_ENCODER_DIR.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n\nbaseline_dev_ndcg = compute_dev_ndcg10(TRAIN_MODEL)\nTRAIN_HISTORY = [{\"epoch\": 0, \"train_loss\": np.nan, \"dev_ndcg_at_10\": baseline_dev_ndcg, \"checkpoint_role\": \"pretrained_baseline\"}]\nbest_dev_ndcg = baseline_dev_ndcg\nbest_epoch = 0\nTRAIN_MODEL.save(str(BEST_ENCODER_DIR))\n\noptimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(\n    TRAIN_MODEL.parameters(), lr=TRAINING_CFG[\"learning_rate\"], weight_decay=TRAINING_CFG[\"weight_decay\"]\n)\nfor epoch in range(1, TRAINING_CFG[\"epochs\"] + 1):\n    TRAIN_MODEL.train()\n    epoch_order = list(range(len(TRAIN_PAIRS)))\n    random.Random(SEED + epoch).shuffle(epoch_order)\n    losses = []\n    for batch_start in tqdm(range(0, len(epoch_order), TRAINING_CFG[\"batch_size\"]), desc=f\"Dense fine-tuning epoch {epoch}\"):\n        batch_indices = epoch_order[batch_start:batch_start + TRAINING_CFG[\"batch_size\"]]\n        if len(batch_indices) < 2:\n            continue\n        batch = [TRAIN_PAIRS[i] for i in batch_indices]\n        query_features = TRAIN_MODEL.tokenize([item[\"query\"] for item in batch])\n        document_features = TRAIN_MODEL.tokenize([item[\"document\"] for item in batch])\n        # Newer Sentence Transformers tokenizers may include non-tensor metadata\n        # (for example, the original text strings) alongside tensor model inputs.\n        # Move tensors only; preserve metadata for modules that pass it through.\n        query_features = {\n            key: value.to(TRAIN_DEVICE) if torch.is_tensor(value) else value\n            for key, value in query_features.items()\n        }\n        document_features = {\n            key: value.to(TRAIN_DEVICE) if torch.is_tensor(value) else value\n            for key, value in document_features.items()\n        }\n        if not any(torch.is_tensor(value) for value in query_features.values()):\n            raise TypeError(\"SentenceTransformer query tokenization returned no tensor inputs\")\n        if not any(torch.is_tensor(value) for value in document_features.values()):\n            raise TypeError(\"SentenceTransformer document tokenization returned no tensor inputs\")\n        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n        query_embeddings = F.normalize(TRAIN_MODEL(query_features)[\"sentence_embedding\"], p=2, dim=1)\n        document_embeddings = F.normalize(TRAIN_MODEL(document_features)[\"sentence_embedding\"], p=2, dim=1)\n        logits = torch.matmul(query_embeddings, document_embeddings.T) / float(TRAINING_CFG[\"temperature\"])\n        labels = torch.arange(len(batch), device=TRAIN_DEVICE)\n        loss = F.cross_entropy(logits, labels)\n        if not torch.isfinite(loss):\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Non-finite dense fine-tuning loss at epoch {epoch}\")\n        loss.backward()\n        torch.nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(TRAIN_MODEL.parameters(), TRAINING_CFG[\"max_grad_norm\"])\n        optimizer.step()\n        losses.append(float(loss.detach().cpu()))\n    if not losses:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"No training batches completed in epoch {epoch}\")\n    dev_score = compute_dev_ndcg10(TRAIN_MODEL)\n    mean_loss = float(np.mean(losses))\n    TRAIN_HISTORY.append({\"epoch\": epoch, \"train_loss\": mean_loss, \"dev_ndcg_at_10\": dev_score, \"checkpoint_role\": \"candidate\"})\n    print(f\"epoch={epoch} | train_loss={mean_loss:.5f} | dev_nDCG@10={dev_score:.5f}\")\n    if dev_score > best_dev_ndcg:\n        best_dev_ndcg = dev_score\n        best_epoch = epoch\n        TRAIN_MODEL.save(str(BEST_ENCODER_DIR))\n\nTRAIN_HISTORY_DF = pd.DataFrame(TRAIN_HISTORY)\nTRAIN_HISTORY_DF.to_csv(RES / \"dense_encoder_training_history.csv\", index=False)\nTRAINING_RECORD = {\n    \"component\": \"dense bi-encoder\",\n    \"base_repository\": MODEL_SPECS[\"embedding\"][\"repo_id\"],\n    \"base_commit_sha\": MODEL_SPECS[\"embedding\"][\"revision\"],\n    \"method\": TRAINING_CFG[\"loss\"], \"epochs_requested\": TRAINING_CFG[\"epochs\"],\n    \"epochs_completed\": len(TRAIN_HISTORY) - 1, \"batch_size\": TRAINING_CFG[\"batch_size\"],\n    \"learning_rate\": TRAINING_CFG[\"learning_rate\"], \"weight_decay\": TRAINING_CFG[\"weight_decay\"],\n    \"temperature\": TRAINING_CFG[\"temperature\"], \"max_grad_norm\": TRAINING_CFG[\"max_grad_norm\"],\n    \"training_query_document_pairs\": len(TRAIN_PAIRS), \"training_queries_skipped\": len(train_skipped_qids),\n    \"unique_positive_documents\": len(set(train_positive_doc_ids)),\n    \"positive_document_collisions\": len(train_positive_doc_ids) - len(set(train_positive_doc_ids)),\n    \"train_split_queries\": len(TRAIN_QRELS), \"development_split_queries\": len(DEV_QRELS),\n    \"test_qrels_accessed_by_training_or_selection\": False,\n    \"development_metric\": \"exact dense retrieval nDCG@10 over fixed_256_overlap32 chunks, parent-document max-score aggregation\",\n    \"baseline_dev_ndcg_at_10\": baseline_dev_ndcg, \"best_epoch_including_baseline\": best_epoch,\n    \"best_dev_ndcg_at_10\": best_dev_ndcg, \"selected_checkpoint_path\": str(BEST_ENCODER_DIR),\n    \"selected_checkpoint_role\": \"pretrained_baseline\" if best_epoch == 0 else \"fine_tuned_epoch\",\n    \"inference_checkpoint_is_pretrained_baseline\": bool(best_epoch == 0),\n    \"checkpoint_selection_candidates\": \"pretrained baseline and each completed training epoch\",\n    \"limitation\": \"In-batch negatives may include an unlabelled relevant document for another query because benchmark qrels may be incomplete.\",\n}\nsave_json(RES / \"dense_encoder_training_config.json\", TRAINING_CFG)\n\ncheckpoint_weight_files = sorted(\n    path for path in BEST_ENCODER_DIR.rglob(\"*\")\n    if path.is_file() and path.suffix in (\".safetensors\", \".bin\", \".pt\", \".pth\")\n)\nif not checkpoint_weight_files:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Fine-tuned dense encoder checkpoint contains no weight files\")\ncheckpoint_hashes = {str(path.relative_to(BEST_ENCODER_DIR)): sha256_file(path) for path in checkpoint_weight_files}\nTRAINING_RECORD[\"checkpoint_weight_sha256\"] = checkpoint_hashes\nTRAINING_RECORD[\"checkpoint_files\"] = [str(path.relative_to(BEST_ENCODER_DIR)) for path in checkpoint_weight_files]\nsave_json(RES / \"dense_encoder_training_summary.json\", TRAINING_RECORD)\n\nMODEL_REVISIONS[\"embedding\"][\"fine_tuning\"] = TRAINING_RECORD\nMODEL_REVISIONS[\"embedding\"][\"inference_checkpoint\"] = str(BEST_ENCODER_DIR)\nMODEL_REVISIONS[\"embedding\"][\"inference_checkpoint_weight_sha256\"] = checkpoint_hashes\nsave_json(RES / \"model_revisions.json\", {\n    \"note\": \"The Hub SHA identifies the initialization checkpoint used for this rerun. The local inference checkpoint is selected using development qrels from the pretrained baseline and completed train-only fine-tuning epochs; when the baseline wins, it remains the inference model. These are not recovered historical-run revisions.\",\n    \"models\": MODEL_REVISIONS,\n})\nEMBEDDING_INFERENCE_PATH = str(BEST_ENCODER_DIR)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(11, 4))\ntrained = TRAIN_HISTORY_DF[TRAIN_HISTORY_DF.epoch > 0]\naxes[0].plot(trained.epoch, trained.train_loss, marker=\"o\")\naxes[0].set(title=\"Dense encoder fine-tuning loss\", xlabel=\"Epoch\", ylabel=\"Mean in-batch contrastive loss\")\naxes[1].plot(TRAIN_HISTORY_DF.epoch, TRAIN_HISTORY_DF.dev_ndcg_at_10, marker=\"s\")\naxes[1].set(title=\"Development checkpoint selection\", xlabel=\"Checkpoint epoch (0 = pretrained)\", ylabel=\"Dev nDCG@10\")\nfig.tight_layout()\nfig.savefig(FIG / \"dense_encoder_training_loss.png\", dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\nplt.close(fig)\n\nMODEL_PROVENANCE_ROWS = []\nfor role, record in MODEL_REVISIONS.items():\n    MODEL_PROVENANCE_ROWS.append({\n        \"role\": role, \"repository\": record[\"repo_id\"], \"base_commit_sha\": record[\"resolved_commit_sha\"],\n        \"base_weight_sha256\": json.dumps(record[\"local_weight_sha256\"], sort_keys=True),\n        \"inference_checkpoint\": record.get(\"inference_checkpoint\", record[\"snapshot_path\"]),\n        \"fine_tuning_executed\": bool(record.get(\"fine_tuning\")),\n        \"selected_checkpoint_role\": record.get(\"fine_tuning\", {}).get(\"selected_checkpoint_role\", \"pretrained_base\"),\n        \"selected_checkpoint_weight_sha256\": json.dumps(record.get(\"inference_checkpoint_weight_sha256\", record[\"local_weight_sha256\"]), sort_keys=True),\n    })\nMODEL_PROVENANCE_DF = pd.DataFrame(MODEL_PROVENANCE_ROWS)\nMODEL_PROVENANCE_DF.to_csv(RES / \"model_provenance.csv\", index=False)\ndisplay(TRAIN_HISTORY_DF.round(5))\ndisplay(MODEL_PROVENANCE_DF)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:55:00.017915Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:55:00.018237Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.210211Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T06:55:00.018207Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.209378Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Loading weights:   0%|          | 0/103 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"df09e8123f09478bbc41e8a662d3c33c"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Batches:   0%|          | 0/53 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"8eb5119490aa481fa83bc8f481fe0923"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Writing model shards:   0%|          | 0/1 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"878df92a7bc44c258f7a6696a92f23e5"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Dense fine-tuning epoch 1:   0%|          | 0/81 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_mi