odel.safetensors\": \"d8148c6d49e0a7925134294...</td>\n      <td>/root/.cache/huggingface/hub/models--cross-enc...</td>\n      <td>False</td>\n      <td>pretrained_base</td>\n      <td>{\"model.safetensors\": \"d8148c6d49e0a7925134294...</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":7},{"id":"cell-017","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 9. Retrieval index construction\n\nThree first-stage methods are evaluated for every chunker: Okapi BM25, exact dense bi-encoder cosine retrieval, and reciprocal-rank fusion (RRF). Dense vectors are L2-normalized and searched by exact inner product; no approximate nearest-neighbor index is used. All chunk hits are aggregated to unique parent documents before scoring. Each parent retains up to three highest-ranked supporting chunk IDs for optional reranking and later evidence provenance.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-018","cell_type":"code","source":"TOKEN_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"\\b\\w+\\b\", re.UNICODE)\ndef lexical_tokens(text):\n    return TOKEN_PATTERN.findall((text or \"\").lower())\n\ndef aggregate_ranked_chunk_hits(query_id, chunk_list, ordered_indices, scores, depth, max_support=3):\n    grouped = {}\n    for idx, score in zip(ordered_indices, scores):\n        chunk = chunk_list[int(idx)]\n        doc_id = chunk[\"parent_doc_id\"]\n        if doc_id not in grouped:\n            if len(grouped) >= depth:\n                break\n            grouped[doc_id] = []\n        if len(grouped[doc_id]) < max_support:\n            grouped[doc_id].append((float(score), chunk[\"chunk_id\"]))\n    documents = []\n    for doc_id, values in grouped.items():\n        values = sorted(values, key=lambda item: (-item[0], item[1]))\n        documents.append({\n            \"query_id\": str(query_id), \"doc_id\": str(doc_id), \"score\": values[0][0],\n            \"supporting_chunk_ids\": [chunk_id for _, chunk_id in values],\n        })\n    documents.sort(key=lambda row: (-row[\"score\"], row[\"doc_id\"]))\n    for rank, row in enumerate(documents, start=1):\n        row[\"rank\"] = rank\n    return documents[:depth]\n\nclass BM25Index:\n    def __init__(self, chunk_list):\n        from rank_bm25 import BM25Okapi\n        self.chunk_list = chunk_list\n        self.index = BM25Okapi([lexical_tokens(c[\"text\"]) for c in chunk_list])\n    def search(self, qid, query, depth):\n        scores = np.asarray(self.index.get_scores(lexical_tokens(query)), dtype=np.float64)\n        if not np.isfinite(scores).all():\n            raise RuntimeError(\"BM25 produced non-finite ranking scores\")\n        order = np.lexsort((np.arange(len(scores)), -scores))\n        return aggregate_ranked_chunk_hits(qid, self.chunk_list, order, scores[order], depth)\n\ndef rrf_fuse(query_id, ranking_lists, k=60, depth=100, max_support_chunks=3):\n    fused = {}\n    for source_index, ranking in enumerate(ranking_lists):\n        for position, row in enumerate(ranking, start=1):\n            doc_id = str(row[\"doc_id\"])\n            entry = fused.setdefault(doc_id, {\n                \"query_id\": str(query_id), \"doc_id\": doc_id, \"score\": 0.0,\n                \"supporting_chunk_ids_by_source\": [[] for _ in ranking_lists],\n            })\n            entry[\"score\"] += 1.0 / (k + int(row.get(\"rank\", position)))\n            entry[\"supporting_chunk_ids_by_source\"][source_index].extend(str(x) for x in row.get(\"supporting_chunk_ids\", []))\n    results = sorted(fused.values(), key=lambda row: (-row[\"score\"], row[\"doc_id\"]))[:depth]\n    for rank, row in enumerate(results, start=1):\n        row[\"rank\"] = rank\n        # Round-robin chunk provenance preserves evidence diversity from both lexical and dense lists.\n        merged_chunks, seen_chunks = [], set()\n        source_lists = row.pop(\"supporting_chunk_ids_by_source\")\n        max_source_depth = max((len(items) for items in source_lists), default=0)\n        for offset in range(max_source_depth):\n            for items in source_lists:\n                if offset < len(items):\n                    chunk_id = items[offset]\n                    if chunk_id not in seen_chunks:\n                        merged_chunks.append(chunk_id)\n                        seen_chunks.add(chunk_id)\n                    if len(merged_chunks) >= max_support_chunks:\n                        break\n            if len(merged_chunks) >= max_support_chunks:\n                break\n        row[\"supporting_chunk_ids\"] = merged_chunks\n    return results\n\n# Deterministic unit tests on synthetic data; these do not enter benchmark results.\n_test_rrf = rrf_fuse(\"q\", [\n    [{\"doc_id\": \"d1\", \"rank\": 1, \"supporting_chunk_ids\": [\"a\"]}, {\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"rank\": 2, \"supporting_chunk_ids\": [\"b\"]}],\n    [{\"doc_id\": \"d2\", \"rank\": 1, \"supporting_chunk_ids\": [\"c\"]}, {\"doc_id\": \"d3\", \"rank\": 2, \"supporting_chunk_ids\": [\"d\"]}],\n], k=60, depth=10)\nassert [r[\"doc_id\"] for r in _test_rrf] == [\"d2\", \"d1\", \"d3\"]\nassert abs(_test_rrf[0][\"score\"] - (1 / 62 + 1 / 61)) < 1e-12\nassert _test_rrf[0][\"supporting_chunk_ids\"] == [\"b\", \"c\"]\nprint(\"RRF rank-fusion and cross-source evidence-diversity unit tests passed.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.211461Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.211857Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.231357Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.211832Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.230451Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"RRF rank-fusion and cross-source evidence-diversity unit tests passed.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":8},{"id":"cell-019","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 10. Retrieval evaluation\n\nAll 323 test queries are scored for every configuration. Each chunker receives BM25, dense, and fused RRF first-stage rankings; each first stage is evaluated both before and after a top-20 cross-encoder reranking pass. The reranker scores up to three supporting chunks per candidate parent and retains the maximum chunk score for that document. Reranking cannot recover documents outside its first-stage top-20 shortlist; this boundary is retained in the run manifest.\n\n**Metric conventions:** recall uses all positive qrels for the query; precision is divided by K; MRR is reciprocal rank of the first positive document; nDCG uses gain `2^grade - 1`; MAP@K is normalized by `min(number_of_positive_documents, K)` to match the supplied manuscript's explicitly stated convention.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-020","cell_type":"code","source":"from math import log2\n\ndef metric_for_query(ranked_doc_ids, qrels_for_query, cutoffs=(1, 5, 10)):\n    seen = set()\n    ranked = []\n    for doc_id in ranked_doc_ids:\n        doc_id = str(doc_id)\n        if doc_id not in seen:\n            ranked.append(doc_id)\n            seen.add(doc_id)\n    positive_grades = {str(d): float(g) for d, g in qrels_for_query.items() if float(g) > 0}\n    result = {}\n    for k in cutoffs:\n        topk = ranked[:k]\n        hits = [doc_id for doc_id in topk if doc_id in positive_grades]\n        result[f\"recall_at_{k}\"] = len(hits) / len(positive_grades) if positive_grades else np.nan\n        result[f\"precision_at_{k}\"] = len(hits) / k\n        result[f\"mrr_at_{k}\"] = next((1.0 / rank for rank, doc_id in enumerate(topk, start=1) if doc_id in positive_grades), 0.0)\n        accumulated_precision = 0.0\n        found = 0\n        for rank, doc_id in enumerate(topk, start=1):\n            if doc_id in positive_grades:\n                found += 1\n                accumulated_precision += found / rank\n        result[f\"map_at_{k}\"] = accumulated_precision / min(len(positive_grades), k) if positive_grades else np.nan\n        dcg = sum((2.0 ** positive_grades.get(doc_id, 0.0) - 1.0) / log2(rank + 1) for rank, doc_id in enumerate(topk, start=1))\n        ideal_grades = sorted(positive_grades.values(), reverse=True)[:k]\n        idcg = sum((2.0 ** grade - 1.0) / log2(rank + 1) for rank, grade in enumerate(ideal_grades, start=1))\n        result[f\"ndcg_at_{k}\"] = dcg / idcg if idcg > 0 else np.nan\n    return result\n\ndef evaluate_rankings(config_id, run_by_query):\n    rows = []\n    for qid in sorted(QUERIES):\n        ranked_ids = [r[\"doc_id\"] for r in run_by_query[qid]]\n        rows.append({\"config_id\": config_id, \"query_id\": qid, **metric_for_query(ranked_ids, QRELS[qid], tuple(CFG[\"cutoffs\"]))})\n    frame = pd.DataFrame(rows)\n    metric_cols = [c for c in frame.columns if c not in (\"config_id\", \"query_id\")]\n    means = frame[metric_cols].mean(numeric_only=True).to_dict()\n    return frame, means\n\nRUNS = {}\nRUN_TIMINGS = {}\nINDEX_TIMINGS = {}\nretrieval_start = time.perf_counter()\nquery_texts = [QUERIES[qid] for qid in QUERY_IDS]\n\nfrom sentence_transformers import SentenceTransformer\nDENSE_DEVICE = \"cuda:0\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\nencoder = SentenceTransformer(EMBEDDING_INFERENCE_PATH, device=DENSE_DEVICE)\nencoder_config = AutoConfig.from_pretrained(MODEL_PATHS[\"embedding\"], local_files_only=True)\nmax_positions = int(getattr(encoder_config, \"max_position_embeddings\", 512))\n# Use at most 384 content tokens plus the encoder's special tokens when its position table allows it.\nencoder.max_seq_length = min(386, max_positions)\nDENSE_SEQUENCE_LENGTH = int(encoder.max_seq_length)\nquery_encode_start = time.perf_counter()\nquery_embeddings = encoder.encode(query_texts, batch_size=CFG[\"retrieval\"][\"dense_batch_size\"], convert_to_numpy=True,\n                                  normalize_embeddings=True, show_progress_bar=True).astype(np.float32)\nquery_encode_seconds = time.perf_counter() - query_encode_start\nif not np.isfinite(query_embeddings).all():\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Dense query embeddings contain non-finite values\")\n\nfor strategy in CFG[\"chunking\"]:\n    name = strategy[\"name\"]\n    chunk_list = CHUNKS[name]\n    print(\"\\nBuilding retrieval indexes for\", name, \"| chunks:\", len(chunk_list))\n    # BM25 lexical index and query-time scoring\n    build_start = time.perf_counter()\n    bm25_index = BM25Index(chunk_list)\n    bm25_build_s = time.perf_counter() - build_start\n    bm25_run = {}\n    bm25_ms = []\n    for qid in tqdm(QUERY_IDS, desc=f\"BM25 {name}\"):\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        bm25_run[qid] = bm25_index.search(qid, QUERIES[qid], CFG[\"candidate_depth\"])\n        bm25_ms.append((time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000)\n    RUNS[f\"{name}__bm25__base\"] = bm25_run\n\n    # Dense chunk vectors and exhaustive exact inner-product search.\n    dense_build_start = time.perf_counter()\n    chunk_embeddings = encoder.encode([c[\"text\"] for c in chunk_list], batch_size=CFG[\"retrieval\"][\"dense_batch_size\"],\n                                      convert_to_numpy=True, normalize_embeddings=True, show_progress_bar=True).astype(np.float32)\n    dense_build_s = time.perf_counter() - dense_build_start\n    if not np.isfinite(chunk_embeddings).all():\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Dense chunk embeddings contain non-finite values for {name}\")\n    norms = np.linalg.norm(chunk_embeddings, axis=1)\n    if not np.allclose(norms, 1.0, atol=1e-3):\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Dense embeddings are not L2 normalized for {name}\")\n    dense_run = {}\n    dense_search_ms = []\n    for j, qid in enumerate(QUERY_IDS):\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        scores = chunk_embeddings @ query_embeddings[j]\n        order = np.lexsort((np.arange(len(scores)), -scores))\n        dense_run[qid] = aggregate_ranked_chunk_hits(qid, chunk_list, order, scores[order], CFG[\"candidate_depth\"])\n        dense_search_ms.append((time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000)\n    RUNS[f\"{name}__dense__base\"] = dense_run\n\n    # Rank-only RRF; no raw BM25/dense score summation.\n    hybrid_run = {}\n    rrf_ms = []\n    for qid in QUERY_IDS:\n        t0 = time.perf_counter()\n        hybrid_run[qid] = rrf_fuse(qid, [bm25_run[qid], dense_run[qid]], CFG[\"rrf_k\"], CFG[\"candidate_depth\"])\n        rrf_ms.append((time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000)\n    RUNS[f\"{name}__hybrid__base\"] = hybrid_run\n\n    bm25_query_ms = float(np.mean(bm25_ms))\n    dense_query_ms = float(query_encode_seconds * 1000 / len(QUERY_IDS) + np.mean(dense_search_ms))\n    hybrid_query_ms = bm25_query_ms + dense_query_ms + float(np.mean(rrf_ms))\n    RUN_TIMINGS[f\"{name}__bm25__base\"] = {\"mean_query_latency_ms\": bm25_query_ms, \"bm25_query_ms\": bm25_query_ms, \"dense_query_ms\": 0.0, \"rrf_query_ms\": 0.0, \"rerank_stage_ms\": 0.0}\n    RUN_TIMINGS[f\"{name}__dense__base\"] = {\"mean_query_latency_ms\": dense_query_ms, \"bm25_query_ms\": 0.0, \"dense_query_ms\": dense_query_ms, \"rrf_query_ms\": 0.0, \"rerank_stage_ms\": 0.0}\n    RUN_TIMINGS[f\"{name}__hybrid__base\"] = {\"mean_query_latency_ms\": hybrid_query_ms, \"bm25_query_ms\": bm25_query_ms, \"dense_query_ms\": dense_query_ms, \"rrf_query_ms\": float(np.mean(rrf_ms)), \"rerank_stage_ms\": 0.0}\n    INDEX_TIMINGS[name] = {\"bm25_index_build_seconds\": bm25_build_s, \"dense_index_build_seconds\": dense_build_s,\n                           \"dense_query_encoding_seconds_total\": query_encode_seconds, \"dense_sequence_length\": DENSE_SEQUENCE_LENGTH}\n    del bm25_index, chunk_embeddings\n    gc.collect()\n    if torch.cuda.is_available():\n        torch.cuda.empty_cache()\n\n# Rerank all nine chunking × first-stage combinations, always from the corresponding top-100 list.\nfrom sentence_transformers import CrossEncoder\nrerank_device = \"cuda:1\" if torch.cuda.device_count() >= 2 else DENSE_DEVICE\nreranker = CrossEncoder(MODEL_PATHS[\"reranker\"], device=rerank_device,\n                        max_length=CFG[\"retrieval\"][\"cross_encoder_max_length\"], trust_remote_code=False)\nfor strategy in CFG[\"chunking\"]:\n    chunk_name = strategy[\"name\"]\n    chunk_lookup = CHUNK_BY_ID[chunk_name]\n    for retriever_name in (\"bm25\", \"dense\", \"hybrid\"):\n        base_id = f\"{chunk_name}__{retriever_name}__base\"\n        reranked_id = f\"{chunk_name}__{retriever_name}__reranked\"\n        reranked_run = {}\n        per_query_rerank_ms = []\n        for qid in tqdm(QUERY_IDS, desc=f\"Rerank {chunk_name}/{retriever_name}\"):\n            candidates = RUNS[base_id][qid][:CFG[\"rerank_depth\"]]\n            pairs, pair_docids = [], []\n            for doc in candidates:\n                for chunk_id in doc.get(\"supporting_chunk_ids\", [])[:CFG[\"rerank_chunks_per_document\"]]:\n                    if chunk_id in chunk_lookup:\n                        pairs.append((QUERIES[qid], chunk_lookup[chunk_id][\"text\"]))\n                        pair_docids.append(doc[\"doc_id\"])\n            t0 = time.perf_counter()\n            if pairs:\n                pair_scores = np.asarray(reranker.predict(pairs, batch_size=CFG[\"retrieval\"][\"reranker_batch_size\"],\n                                                          convert_to_numpy=True, show_progress_bar=False), dtype=float).reshape(-1)\n                if len(pair_scores) != len(pairs) or not np.isfinite(pair_scores).all():\n                    raise RuntimeError(f\"Cross-encoder returned malformed/non-finite scores for {reranked_id}/{qid}\")\n            else:\n                pair_scores = np.asarray([], dtype=float)\n            per_query_rerank_ms.append((time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000)\n            score_by_doc = defaultdict(list)\n            for doc_id, score in zip(pair_docids, pair_scores):\n                score_by_doc[doc_id].append(float(score))\n            docs_by_id = {d[\"doc_id\"]: d for d in candidates}\n            scored_docs = []\n            for doc_id, values in score_by_doc.items():\n                entry = dict(docs_by_id[doc_id])\n                entry[\"first_stage_score\"] = float(entry[\"score\"])\n                entry[\"score\"] = max(values)\n                scored_docs.append(entry)\n            scored_docs.sort(key=lambda row: (-row[\"score\"], row[\"doc_id\"]))\n            for rank, row in enumerate(scored_docs, start=1):\n                row[\"rank\"] = rank\n            reranked_run[qid] = scored_docs[:CFG[\"rerank_depth\"]]\n        RUNS[reranked_id] = reranked_run\n        base_latency = RUN_TIMINGS[base_id][\"mean_query_latency_ms\"]\n        rerank_latency = float(np.mean(per_query_rerank_ms))\n        base_parts = dict(RUN_TIMINGS[base_id])\n        RUN_TIMINGS[reranked_id] = {**base_parts, \"rerank_stage_ms\": rerank_latency,\n                                    \"mean_query_latency_ms\": base_latency + rerank_latency}\n\nreranker = None\nencoder = None\ngc.collect()\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    torch.cuda.empty_cache()\nprint(f\"Retrieval sweep completed in {(time.perf_counter() - retrieval_start) / 60:.1f} minutes.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.232764Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.233755Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T07:04:19.662339Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T06:58:43.233728Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T07:04:19.661393Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Loading weights:   0%|          | 0/103 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"f0bbd97af8bf44039069d79192172dc3"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Batches:   0%|          | 0/3 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"6a827a745f3740a8b7664d0ad82e641e"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"\nBuilding retrieval indexes for fixed_128 | chunks: 11314\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"BM25 fixed_128:   0%|          | 0/323 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"fdf46b1558f344538f29079c91