ng the final prompt.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-026","cell_type":"code","source":"from transformers import AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM\nGEN_TOKENIZER = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_PATHS[\"generator\"], local_files_only=True)\nGEN_DEVICE = \"cuda:0\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\"\nGENERATOR = AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained(\n    MODEL_PATHS[\"generator\"], local_files_only=True, dtype=torch.float32,\n    use_safetensors=True if (Path(MODEL_PATHS[\"generator\"]) / \"model.safetensors\").exists() else False,\n).to(GEN_DEVICE).eval()\nif next(GENERATOR.parameters()).dtype != torch.float32:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Primary generator must be loaded in FP32.\")\n\nTOK_LIMIT = getattr(GEN_TOKENIZER, \"model_max_length\", None)\ntry:\n    TOK_LIMIT = int(TOK_LIMIT)\nexcept Exception:\n    TOK_LIMIT = None\nif TOK_LIMIT is None or TOK_LIMIT <= 0 or TOK_LIMIT > 1_000_000:\n    TOK_LIMIT = getattr(GENERATOR.config, \"n_positions\", None) or getattr(GENERATOR.config, \"max_source_positions\", None)\nif TOK_LIMIT is None:\n    raise RuntimeError(\"The generator's declared input-token limit could not be established; refusing to guess.\")\nTOK_LIMIT = int(TOK_LIMIT)\n\nGENERATOR_INFO = {\n    \"repo_id\": MODEL_SPECS[\"generator\"][\"repo_id\"], \"commit_sha\": MODEL_REVISIONS[\"generator\"][\"resolved_commit_sha\"],\n    \"device\": GEN_DEVICE, \"dtype\": str(next(GENERATOR.parameters()).dtype), \"autocast\": False,\n    \"tokenizer_declared_input_limit\": TOK_LIMIT, \"max_new_tokens\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"max_new_tokens\"], \"min_new_tokens\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"min_new_tokens\"],\n    \"min_answer_words\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"min_answer_words\"],\n    \"do_sample\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"do_sample\"], \"num_beams\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"num_beams\"],\n    \"num_return_sequences\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"num_return_sequences\"],\n    \"early_stopping\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"early_stopping\"], \"length_penalty\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"length_penalty\"],\n    \"no_repeat_ngram_size\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"no_repeat_ngram_size\"],\n    \"repetition_penalty\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"repetition_penalty\"],\n    \"pad_token_id\": GEN_TOKENIZER.pad_token_id, \"eos_token_id\": GEN_TOKENIZER.eos_token_id,\n    \"parameter_count\": sum(p.numel() for p in GENERATOR.parameters()),\n}\nprint(json.dumps(GENERATOR_INFO, indent=2))\nsave_json(RES / \"generator_runtime.json\", GENERATOR_INFO)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T07:04:26.045558Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T07:04:26.046303Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.702811Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T07:04:26.04628Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.702056Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Loading weights:   0%|          | 0/558 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"b4b3304b6b4d4d2d9251379663c8e3bb"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stderr","text":"[transformers] The tied weights mapping and config for this model specifies to tie shared.weight to lm_head.weight, but both are present in the checkpoints with different values, so we will NOT tie them. You should update the config with `tie_word_embeddings=False` to silence this warning.\n","output_type":"stream"},{"name":"stdout","text":"{\n  \"repo_id\": \"google/flan-t5-large\",\n  \"commit_sha\": \"0613663d0d48ea86ba8cb3d7a44f0f65dc596a2a\",\n  \"device\": \"cuda:0\",\n  \"dtype\": \"torch.float32\",\n  \"autocast\": false,\n  \"tokenizer_declared_input_limit\": 512,\n  \"max_new_tokens\": 128,\n  \"min_new_tokens\": 8,\n  \"min_answer_words\": 5,\n  \"do_sample\": false,\n  \"num_beams\": 4,\n  \"num_return_sequences\": 1,\n  \"early_stopping\": true,\n  \"length_penalty\": 1.0,\n  \"no_repeat_ngram_size\": 3,\n  \"repetition_penalty\": 1.08,\n  \"pad_token_id\": 0,\n  \"eos_token_id\": 1,\n  \"parameter_count\": 783150080\n}\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":12},{"id":"cell-027","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 14. Evidence-context construction\n\nThe generator sees neutral passage labels (`Passage 1`, etc.) and passage text only. Document IDs and chunk IDs are stored outside the prompt for auditability. The builder iteratively fits the question, instructions, labels, and selected passages within the tokenizer's declared input limit. It records exactly which evidence text was supplied, including any truncation.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-028","cell_type":"code","source":"def token_count(text):\n    # Count the exact model input, including tokenizer-added special tokens.\n    return len(GEN_TOKENIZER.encode(text, add_special_tokens=True))\n\ndef compose_prompt(query, passage_blocks, instruction):\n    evidence_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(passage_blocks) if passage_blocks else \"[No retrieved evidence]\"\n    return f\"{instruction}\\n\\nInformation need: {query}\\n\\nEvidence passages:\\n{evidence_text}\\n\\nWrite the answer as one or two complete sentences:\"\n\n\n\ndef compose_recovery_prompt(query, evidence_texts, instruction):\n    \"\"\"Build the single permitted retry prompt from the exact same evidence text, without passage labels.\"\"\"\n    clean_evidence = [str(text).strip() for text in evidence_texts if str(text).strip()]\n    if not clean_evidence:\n        raise ValueError(\"Recovery requires at least one non-empty evidence excerpt.\")\n    evidence_block = \"\\n\\n---\\n\\n\".join(clean_evidence)\n    return (\n        f\"{instruction.strip()}\\n\\n\"\n        f\"Source excerpts:\\n{evidence_block}\\n\\n\"\n        f\"Information need:\\n{query.strip()}\\n\\n\"\n        \"Complete sentence(s):\"\n    )\n\n\ndef compose_recovery_prompt_2(query, evidence_texts, instruction):\n    \"\"\"Second (final) permitted retry: question-answering form over the same evidence.\"\"\"\n    clean_evidence = [str(text).strip() for text in evidence_texts if str(text).strip()]\n    if not clean_evidence:\n        raise ValueError(\"Recovery requires at least one non-empty evidence excerpt.\")\n    evidence_block = \"\\n\\n\".join(clean_evidence)\n    return (\n        f\"{instruction.strip()}\\n\\n\"\n        f\"Source excerpts:\\n{evidence_block}\\n\\n\"\n        f\"Question: What do the source excerpts report about \\\"{query.strip()}\\\"?\\n\\n\"\n        \"One-sentence answer:\"\n    )\n\ndef build_evidence_prompt(query, ranked_documents, chunk_lookup, instruction=None):\n    instruction = instruction or CFG[\"generation\"][\"prompt_instruction\"]\n    suffix_probe = compose_prompt(query, [], instruction)\n    if token_count(suffix_probe) > TOK_LIMIT:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"The fixed generation instruction and query exceed the model input limit.\")\n    evidence_items = []\n    used_chunk_ids = set()\n    for doc in ranked_documents:\n        for chunk_id in doc.get(\"supporting_chunk_ids\", []):\n            if chunk_id in used_chunk_ids or chunk_id not in chunk_lookup:\n                continue\n            chunk = chunk_lookup[chunk_id]\n            if len(evidence_items) >= CFG[\"generation\"][\"top_passages\"]:\n                break\n            next_label = f\"Passage {len(evidence_items) + 1}: \"\n            token_ids = GEN_TOKENIZER.encode(chunk[\"text\"], add_special_tokens=False)\n            if not token_ids:\n                continue\n            low, high, best_text = 1, len(token_ids), \"\"\n            while low <= high:\n                mid = (low + high) // 2\n                candidate_text = GEN_TOKENIZER.decode(token_ids[:mid], skip_special_tokens=True, clean_up_tokenization_spaces=False).strip()\n                candidate_blocks = [item[\"prompt_block\"] for item in evidence_items] + [next_label + candidate_text]\n                candidate_prompt = compose_prompt(query, candidate_blocks, instruction)\n                if token_count(candidate_prompt) <= TOK_LIMIT:\n                    best_text = candidate_text\n                    low = mid + 1\n                else:\n                    high = mid - 1\n            if len(GEN_TOKENIZER.encode(best_text, add_special_tokens=False)) < 8:\n                continue\n            prompt_block = next_label + best_text\n            evidence_items.append({\n                \"doc_id\": chunk[\"parent_doc_id\"], \"chunk_id\": chunk_id,\n                \"doc_rank\": int(doc.get(\"rank\", 0)), \"text\": best_text,\n                \"prompt_label\": f\"Passage {len(evidence_items) + 1}\",\n                \"truncated_to_fit\": len(GEN_TOKENIZER.encode(best_text, add_special_tokens=False)) < len(token_ids),\n                \"prompt_block\": prompt_block,\n            })\n            used_chunk_ids.add(chunk_id)\n        if len(evidence_items) >= CFG[\"generation\"][\"top_passages\"]:\n            break\n    final_prompt = compose_prompt(query, [item[\"prompt_block\"] for item in evidence_items], instruction)\n    final_tokens = token_count(final_prompt)\n    if final_tokens > TOK_LIMIT:\n        raise AssertionError(f\"Prompt builder exceeded declared input limit: {final_tokens} > {TOK_LIMIT}\")\n    for item in evidence_items:\n        item.pop(\"prompt_block\", None)\n    return {\"prompt\": final_prompt, \"evidence\": evidence_items, \"input_tokens\": final_tokens,\n            \"input_limit\": TOK_LIMIT, \"evidence_passage_count\": len(evidence_items)}","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.705771Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.706169Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.720259Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.706143Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.719442Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":13},{"id":"cell-029","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 15. Generation, output validation, and score diagnostics\n\nGeneration uses deterministic four-beam FP32 decoding (sampling disabled). Every attempt stores the exact prompt, raw decoded output, token counts, latency, score-tensor diagnostics, status, and error details. NaN, positive-infinity, malformed score tensors, and all-masked score rows invalidate an attempt. Negative-infinity values are allowed as normal constrained-decoding masks. Empty outputs, factual answers shorter than the configured five-word minimum, exact query/prompt echoes, generic placeholder labels, and evidence-metadata echoes are never marked successful. A clear, complete evidence-insufficient abstention is accepted even when it is shorter than five words. NFCorpus keyword-style queries are treated as information needs; generation must state a concrete evidence-supported finding rather than return the topic label. Calibration controls separately permit one-word answers. RAG generation uses a minimum of eight new tokens to reduce bare-heading and topic-label outputs; calibration controls override this to one new token.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-030","cell_type":"code","source":"STATUS_COMPLETED = \"COMPLETED\"\nSTATUS_EMPTY = \"EMPTY_OUTPUT\"\nSTATUS_INVALID = \"INVALID_OUTPUT\"\nSTATUS_FAILED = \"FAILED_GENERATION\"\nEVIDENCE_META_PATTERN = re.compile(r\"\\b(doc_id|chunk_id|document_id)\\b|passage\\s*\\d+\\s*:|evidence passages:|question:\", re.I)\nABSTENTION_PATTERN = re.compile(\n    r\"^(?:the )?(?:(?:retrieved|supplied|provided) )?evidence is insufficient\"\n    r\"(?: to answer (?:this|the) (?:question|topic))?[.!]?$|\"\n    r\"^(?:the )?(?:(?:retrieved|supplied|provided) )?excerpts do not provide enough information\"\n    r\"(?: to answer (?:this|the) (?:question|topic))?[.!]?$|\"\n    r\"^(?:there is )?not enough (?:evidence|information)(?: in the (?:retrieved|supplied) excerpts)?[.!]?$|\"\n    r\"^insufficient evidence[.!]?$\",\n    re.I,\n)\nPLACEHOLDER_ANSWER_PATTERN = re.compile(\n    r\"^(?:evidence[- ]grounded(?: answer)?|answer|response|evidence[- ]based answer)[\\s:.,;!-]*$\",\n    re.I,\n)\nECHO_SUFFIX_TOKENS = {\"evidence\", \"grounded\", \"answer\", \"response\", \"finding\", \"summary\"}\n\ndef _normalize_answer_for_comparison(text):\n    return re.sub(r\"\\W+\", \" \", (text or \"\").casefold()).strip()\n\ndef validate_answer_text(answer, prompt, query, min_words=1):\n    text = (answer or \"\").strip()\n    if not text:\n        return False, STATUS_EMPTY, \"decoded answer is empty\"\n    low = text.casefold()\n    normalized_q = _normalize_answer_for_comparison(query)\n    normalized_a = _normalize_answer_for_comparison(text)\n    if \"evidence passages:\" in low or \"question:\" in low or \"answer:\" in low:\n        return False, STATUS_INVALID, \"prompt structure echoed\"\n    if EVIDENCE_META_PATTERN.search(text):\n        return False, STATUS_INVALID, \"evidence label or metadata echoed\"\n    # Reject exact query echoes regardless of word count or punctuation.\n    if normalized_q and normalized_a == normalized_q:\n        return False, STATUS_INVALID, \"question echoed\"\n    # Reject a topic copied and followed only by a generic model/prompt label.\n    if normalized_q and normalized_a.startswith(normalized_q + \" \"):\n        suffix = normalized_a[len(normalized_q):].strip().split()\n        if suffix and all(token in ECHO_SUFFIX_TOKENS for token in suffix):\n            return False, STATUS_INVALID, \"question followed by a generic label\"\n    if PLACEHOLDER_ANSWER_PATTERN.fullmatch(text):\n        return False, STATUS_INVALID, \"generic answer placeholder\"\n    if prompt.strip() and normalized_a == _normalize_answer_for_comparison(prompt):\n        return False, STATUS_INVALID, \"full prompt echoed\"\n    # A clear, complete abstention is valid even when shorter than the factual-answer minimum.\n    if ABSTENTION_PATTERN.fullmatch(text):\n        return True, STATUS_COMPLETED, None\n    words = re.findall(r\"\\b[\\w'-]+\\b\", text, flags=re.UNICODE)\n    if len(words) < int(min_words):\n        return False, STATUS_INVALID, f\"fewer than {int(min_words)} words for a factual answer\"\n    return True, STATUS_COMPLETED, None\n\ndef evidence_metadata_echo(answer, evidence_items):\n    \"\"\"Detect literal parent/chunk identifiers echoed from the audit metadata.\"\"\"\n    answer_folded = (answer or \"\").casefold()\n    for item in evidence_items:\n        for field in (\"doc_id\", \"chunk_id\"):\n            identifier = str(item.get(field, \"\")).strip()\n            if len(identifier) >= 5 and identifier.casefold() in answer_folded:\n                return identifier\n    return None\n\ndef check_generation_scores(score_steps, expected_rows=None):\n    expected_rows = int(expected_rows if expected_rows is not None else CFG[\"generation\"][\"num_beams\"])\n    diagnostics = {\"score_steps\": 0, \"expected_score_rows\": expected_rows, \"score_tensor_shapes_valid\": True, \"nan_count\": 0,\n                   \"positive_infinity_count\": 0, \"negative_infinity_count\": 0,\n                   \"all_masked_rows\": 0, \"score_checks_passed\": True}\n    if score_steps is None or len(score_steps) == 0:\n        diagnostics.update(score_tensor_shapes_valid=False, score_checks_passed=False, error=\"no generation score tensors returned\")\n        return diagnostics\n    for step_index, score in enumerate(score_steps):\n        diagnostics[\"score_steps\"] += 1\n        if not torch.is_tensor(score) or score.ndim != 2 or score.shape[0] != expected_rows or score.shape[1] <= 0:\n            diagnostics[\"score_tensor_shapes_valid\"] = False\n            diagnostics[\"score_checks_passed\"] = False\n            observed = tuple(score.shape) if torch.is_tensor(score) else type(score).__name__\n            diagnostics[\"error\"] = f\"malformed score tensor at step {step_index}: observed={observed}, expected_rows={expected_rows}\"\n            break\n        diagnostics[\"nan_count\"] += int(torch.isnan(score).sum().item())\n        diagnostics[\"positive_infinity_count\"] += int(torch.isposinf(score).sum().item())\n        diagnostics[\"negative_infinity_count\"] += int(torch.isneginf(score).sum().item())\n        diagnostics[\"all_masked_rows\"] += int((~torch.isfinite(score)).all(dim=-1).sum().item())\n    if diagnostics[\"nan_count\"] or diagnostics[\"positive_infinity_count\"] or diagnostics[\"all_masked_rows\"]:\n        diagnostics[\"score_checks_passed\"] = False\n    return diagnostics\n\ndef generate_attempt(prompt, query, attempt_number, condition_id, query_id, recovery=False, min_answer_words=None, min_new_tokens=None):\n    if min_answer_words is None:\n        min_answer_words = int(CFG[\"generation\"].get(\"min_answer_words\", 5))\n    min_answer_words = int(min_answer_words)\n    if min_new_tokens is None:\n        min_new_tokens = int(CFG[\"generation\"].get(\"min_new_tokens\", 1))\n    min_new_tokens = int(min_new_tokens)\n    record = {\"condition\": condition_id, \"query_id\": query_id, \"attempt\": attempt_number,\n              \"recovery\": bool(recovery), \"prompt\": prompt, \"input_tokens\": token_count(prompt),\n              \"input_limit\": TOK_LIMIT, \"model_dtype\": str(next(GENERATOR.parameters()).dtype),\n              \"autocast_used\": False, \"max_new_tokens\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"max_new_tokens\"], \"min_new_tokens\": min_new_tokens,\n              \"do_sample\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"do_sample\"], \"num_beams\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"num_beams\"],\n              \"num_return_sequences\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"num_return_sequences\"],\n              \"early_stopping\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"early_stopping\"],\n              \"length_penalty\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"length_penalty\"],\n              \"no_repeat_ngram_size\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"no_repeat_ngram_size\"],\n              \"repetition_penalty\": CFG[\"generation\"][\"repetition_penalty\"],\n              \"min_answer_words\": min_answer_words,\n              \"answer\": \"\", \"status\": STATUS_FAILED,\n              \"error\": None, \"latency_ms\": np.nan}\n    if record[\"input_tokens\"] > TOK_LIMIT:\n        record.update(status=STATUS_FAILED, error=f\"prompt exceeds input limit: {record['input_tokens']} > {TOK_LIMIT}\")\n        record.update(check_generation_scores(None))\n        return record\n    encoded = GEN_TOKENIZER(prompt, return_tensors=\"pt\", truncation=False)\n    encoded = {k: v.to(GEN_DEVICE) for k, v in encoded.items()}\n    if torch.cuda.is_available() and str(GEN_DEVICE).startswith(\"cuda\"):\n        torch.cuda.synchronize()\n    started = time.perf_counter()\n    try:\n        with torch.inference_mode():\n            output = GENERATOR.generate(\n                **encoded,\n                max_new_tokens=CFG[\"generation\"][\"max_new_tokens\"],\n                min_new_tokens=min_new_tokens,\n                do_sample=CFG[\"generation\"][\"do_sample\"],\n                num_beams=CFG[\"generation\"][\"num_beams\"],\n                num_return_sequences=CFG[\"generation\"][\"num_return_sequences\"],\n                early_stopping=CFG[\"generation\"][\"early_stopping\"],\n                length_penalty=CFG[\"generation\"][\"length_penalty\"],\n                no_repeat_ngram_size=CFG[\"generation\"][\"no_repeat_ngram_size\"],\n                repetition_penalty=CFG[\"generation\"][\"repetition_penalty\"],\n                return_dict_in_generate=True,\n                output_scores=True,\n            )\n        if torch.cuda.is_available() and str(GEN_DEVICE).startswith(\"cuda\"):\n            torch.cuda.synchronize()\n        record[\"latency_ms\"] = (time.perf_counter() - started) * 1000\n        score_info = check_generation_scores(getattr(output, \"scores\", None), expected_rows=CFG[\"generation\"][\"num_beams\"])\n        record.update(score_info)\n        sequences = output.sequences.detach().cpu()\n        if sequences.ndim != 2 or sequences.shape[0] != 1:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"unexpected sequence output shape: {tuple(sequences.shape)}\")\n        output_ids = [int(x) for x in sequences[0].tolist()]\n        decoded = GEN_TOKENIZER.decode(output_ids, skip_special_tokens=True, clean_up_tokenization_spaces=True).strip()\n        record[\"generated_token_ids\"] = output_ids\n        record[\"generated_sequence_token_count\"] = len(output_ids)\n        record[\"output_token_count\"] = len(GEN_TOKENIZER.encode(decoded, add_special_tokens=False))\n        record[\"answer\"] = decoded\n        valid, status, reason = validate_answer_text(decoded, prompt, query, min_words=min_answer_words)\n        if not record[\"score_checks_passed\"]:\n            valid, status, reason = False, STATUS_INVALID, \"generation score diagnostics failed\"\n        record.update(answer_valid=bool(valid), status=status, invalid_reason=reason)\n    except Exception as exc:\n        record.update(status=STATUS_FAILED, error=repr(exc), answer=\"\", answer_valid=False)\n        record.update(check_generation_scores(None))\n    return record","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.721335Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.72194Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.749172Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.721909Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.748405Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":14},{"id":"cell-031","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 16. Diagnostics and calibration controls\n\nTwo small generator controls check that the pinned model actually emits text. Their expected keywords are diagnostic only; they are not part of the biomedical test set and do not tune the model, prompts, thresholds, or retrieval configuration. The primary experiment remains evidence-bounded RAG generation.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-032","cell_type":"code","source":"CALIBRATION_CONTROLS = [\n    {\"control_id\": \"CTRL_CAPITAL\", \"prompt\": \"Respond with only the city name. What is the capital of France?\", \"expected_keyword\": \"Paris\"},\n    {\"control_id\": \"CTRL_WATER_FORMULA\", \"prompt\": \"Respond with only the chemical formula. What is the chemical formula for water?\", \"expected_keyword\": \"H2O\"},\n]\nCALIBRATION_ROWS = []\nfor control in CALIBRATION_CONTROLS:\n    # No answer is supplied to the model; only the prompt and scoring rule are predefined.\n    # Diagnostic controls may legitimately be one-token answers (e.g., Paris or H2O).\n    # The factual-answer minimum applies to RAG outputs; explicit evidence-insufficient abstentions are separately accepted.\n    control_row = generate_attempt(control[\"prompt\"], control[\"prompt\"], 1, \"CALIBRATION\", control[\"control_id\"], recovery=False, min_answer_words=1, min_new_tokens=1)\n    CALIBRATION_ROWS.append({\n        \"control_id\": control[\"control_id\"], \"prompt\": control[\"prompt\"],\n        \"expected_keyword_diagnostic_only\": control[\"expected_keyword\"],\n        \"actual_model_output\": control_row.get(\"answer\", \"\"), \"status\": control_row.get(\"status\"),\n        \"keyword_match_diagnostic_only\": control[\"expected_keyword\"].casefold() in str(control_row.get(\"answer\", \"\")).casefold(),\n        \"latency_ms\": control_row.get(\"latency_ms\"), \"score_checks_passed\": control_row.get(\"score_checks_passed\", False),\n        \"error\": control_row.get(\"error\"),\n    })\nCALIBRATION_DF = pd.DataFrame(CALIBRATION_ROWS)\nCALIBRATION_DF.to_csv(RES / \"calibration_control_outputs.csv\", index=False)\ndisplay(CALIBRATION_DF)\nif not (CALIBRATION_DF[\"status\"] == STATUS_COMPLETED).all():\n    save_json(REP / \"preflight_failure.json\", {\"reason\": \"At least one generator calibration control failed to produce a valid output.\", \"rows\": CALIBRATION_ROWS})\n    raise RuntimeError(\"Generator preflight failed; the full RAG generation run is stopped.\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.750185Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.750485Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T07:04:29.180644Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T07:04:27.750455Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T07:04:29.179966Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"           control_id                                             prompt  \\\n0        CTRL_CAPITAL  Respond with only the city name. What is the c...   \n1  CTRL_WATER_FORMULA  Respond with only the chemical formula. What i...   \n\n  expected_keyword_diagnostic_only actual_model_output     status  \\\n0                            Paris               paris  COMPLETED   \n1                              H2O                   w  COMPLETED   \n\n   keyword_match_diagnostic_only   latency_ms  score_checks_passed error  \n0                           True  1068.736463                 True  None  \n1                          False   318.971221                 True  None  ","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>control_id</th>\n      <th>prompt</th>\n      <th>expected_keyword_diagnostic_only</th>\n      <th>actual_model_output</th>\n      <th>status</th>\n      <th>keyword_match_diagnostic_only</th>\n      <th>latency_ms</th>\n      <th>score_checks_passed</th>\n      <th>error</th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>0</th>\n      <td>CTRL_CAPITAL</td>\n      <td>Respond with only the city name. What is the c...</td>\n      <td>Paris</td>\n      <td>paris</td>\n      <td>COMPLETED</td>\n      <td>True</td>\n      <td>1068.736463</td>\n      <td>True</td>\n      <td>None</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>1</th>\n      <td>CTRL_WATER_FORMULA</td>\n      <td>Respond with only the chemical formula. What i...</td>\n      <td>H2O</td>\n      <td>w</td>\n      <td>COMPLETED</td>\n      <td>False</td>\n      <td>318.971221</td>\n      <td>True</td>\n      <td>None</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":15},{"id":"cell-033","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 17. Full answer generation\n\nEach condition uses its corresponding retrieval ranking and the same 100 sampled query IDs. A first invalid/empty generation receives up to **two** logged recovery attempts with the **same evidence passages** and different, pre-declared prompt wrappers (a plain restatement, then a question-answer form). Factual benchmark answers must contain at least five words; clear, complete evidence-insufficient abstentions are valid even when shorter. Calibration controls retain their separate one-word rule. If the last recovery attempt is also invalid, the final output remains invalid; no template answer or manual fallback is inserted. Results are checkpointed during generation so a runtime interruption leaves an auditable record.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-034","cell_type":"code","source":"GEN_CONDITION_TO_RUN = {\n    \"C1_fixed128_bm25\": \"fixed_128__bm25__base\",\n    \"C2_fixed256o32_hybrid\": \"fixed_256_overlap32__hybrid__base\",\n    \"C3_fixed256o32_hybrid_rerank\": \"fixed_256_overlap32__hybrid__reranked\",\n}\nGEN_CONDITION_LOOKUP = {c[\"id\"]: c for c in GEN_CONDITIONS}\nATTEMPT_ROWS = []\nFINAL_OUTPUT_ROWS = []\nATTEMPT_JSONL = RES / \"generation_attempts.jsonl\"\nOUTPUT_JSONL = RES / \"generation_outputs.jsonl\"\nfor path in (ATTEMPT_JSONL, OUTPUT_JSONL):\n    if path.exists():\n        path.unlink()\n\ndef finalize_attempt(attempt, prompt_package, retrieved_doc_ids, n_tokens):\n    attempt[\"evidence\"] = prompt_package[\"evidence\"]\n    echo = evidence_metadata_echo(attempt.get(\"answer\", \"\"), prompt_package[\"evidence\"])\n    if echo:\n        attempt.update(answer_valid=False, status=STATUS_INVALID, invalid_reason=\"document/chunk identifier echoed from audit metadata\")\n    attempt[\"evidence_metadata_echo\"] = echo\n    attempt[\"retrieved_doc_ids\"] = retrieved_doc_ids\n    attempt[\"input_tokens\"] = n_tokens\n    return attempt\n\nwith open(ATTEMPT_JSONL, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as attempt_stream, open(OUTPUT_JSONL, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as output_stream:\n    for condition in GEN_CONDITIONS:\n        condition_id = condition[\"id\"]\n        run_id = GEN_CONDITION_TO_RUN[condition_id]\n        chunk_lookup = CHUNK_BY_ID[condition[\"chunking\"]]\n        for qid in tqdm(SAMPLE_IDS, desc=f\"Generate {condition_id}\"):\n            ranked_docs = RUNS[run_id][qid]\n            prompt_package = build_evidence_prompt(QUERIES[qid], ranked_docs, chunk_lookup, CFG[\"generation\"][\"prompt_instruction\"])\n            if not prompt_package[\"evidence\"]:\n                raise RuntimeError(f\"No evidence passage could be constructed for {condition_id}/{qid}; refusing to generate without evidence provenance.\")\n            retrieved_doc_ids = [r[\"doc_id\"] for r in ranked_docs]\n            evidence_texts = [e[\"text\"] for e in prompt_package[\"evidence\"]]\n            attempt_1 = generate_attempt(prompt_package[\"prompt\"], QUERIES[qid], 1, condition_id, qid, recovery=False,\n                                         min_answer_words=CFG[\"generation\"][\"min_answer_words\"])\n            finalize_attempt(attempt_1, prompt_package, retrieved_doc_ids, prompt_package[\"input_tokens\"])\n            ATTEMPT_ROWS.append(attempt_1)\n            attempt_stream.write(json.dumps(attempt_1, ensure_ascii=False, default=str) + \"\\n\")\n            attempts_for_query = [attempt_1]\n            final_attempt = attempt_1\n            # Up to max_recovery_attempts logged retries with the SAME evidence text and a different, pre-declared wrapper.\n            recovery_builders = [\n                (compose_recovery_prompt, CFG[\"generation\"][\"recovery_instruction\"]),\n                (compose_recovery_prompt_2, CFG[\"generation\"][\"recovery_instruction_2\"]),\n            ][:CFG[\"generation\"][\"max_recovery_attempts\"]]\n            for number, (builder, instruction) in enumerate(recovery_builders, start=2):\n                if final_attempt[\"status\"] not in (STATUS_EMPTY, STATUS_INVALID):\n                    break\n                recovery_prompt = builder(QUERIES[qid], evidence_texts, instruction)\n                recovery_tokens = token_count(recovery_prompt)\n                if recovery_tokens > TOK_LIMIT:\n                    raise RuntimeError(f\"Recovery prompt exceeds generator input limit for {condition_id}/{qid}: {recovery_tokens} > {TOK_LIMIT}\")\n                retry = generate_attempt(recovery_prompt, QUERIES[qid], number, condition_id, qid, recovery=True,\n                                         min_answer_words=CFG[\"generation\"][\"min_answer_words\"])\n                finalize_attempt(retry, prompt_package, retrieved_doc_ids, recovery_tokens)\n                ATTEMPT_ROWS.append(retry)\n                attempt_stream.write(json.dumps(retry, ensure_ascii=False, default=str) + \"\\n\")\n                attempts_for_query.append(retry)\n                final_attempt = retry\n            final_row = {\n                \"condition\": condition_id, \"query_id\": qid, \"query\": QUERIES[qid],\n                \"answer\": final_attempt.get(\"answer\", \"\"), \"status\": final_attempt.get(\"status\"),\n                \"answer_valid\": bool(final_attempt.get(\"answer_valid\", False)),\n                \"invalid_reason\": final_attempt.get(\"invalid_reason\"), \"error\": final_attempt.get(\"error\"),\n                \"final_attempt_number\": final_attempt.get(\"attempt\"), \"recovery_used\": len(attempts_for_query) > 1,\n                \"n_attempts\": len(attempts_for_query),\n                \"latency_ms\": float(sum(float(a.get(\"latency_ms\") or 0.0) for a in attempts_for_query)),\n                \"input_tokens\": final_attempt.get(\"input_tokens\"), \"input_limit\": TOK_LIMIT,\n                \"output_token_count\": final_attempt.get(\"output_token_count\"),\n                \"evidence\": prompt_package[\"evidence\"], \"retrieved_doc_ids\": retrieved_doc_ids,\n                \"evidence_passage_count\": len(prompt_package[\"evidence\"]),\n                \"evidence_metadata_echo\": final_attempt.get(\"evidence_metadata_echo\"),\n                \"prompt\": final_attempt.get(\"prompt\"),\n                \"generation_score_checks_passed\": bool(final_attempt.get(\"score_checks_passed\", False)),\n            }\n            FINAL_OUTPUT_ROWS.append(final_row)\n            output_stream.write(json.dumps(final_row, ensure_ascii=False, default=str) + \"\\n\")\n            output_stream.flush()\n            attempt_stream.flush()\n\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS = pd.DataFrame(ATTEMPT_ROWS)\nGENERATION_OUTPUTS = pd.DataFrame(FINAL_OUTPUT_ROWS)\nGENERATION_ATTEMPTS.to_csv(RES / \"generation_attempts.csv\", index=False)\nGENERATION_OUTPUTS.to_csv(RES / \"generation_outputs.csv\", index=False)\nprint(\"Final outputs:\", len(GENERATION_OUTPUTS), \"| generation attempts including recoveries:\", len(GENERATION_ATTEMPTS))\nprint(GENERATION_OUTPUTS.groupby([\"condition\", \"status\"]).size().unstack(fill_value=0))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T07:04:29.181654Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T07:04:29.182302Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.655649Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T07:04:29.182274Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.654784Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Generate C1_fixed128_bm25:   0%|          | 0/100 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"e1a3fda3e09c48be915d92516b8299ce"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stderr","text":"[transformers] Token indices sequence length is longer than the specified maximum sequence length for this model (542 > 512). Running this sequence through the model will result in indexing errors\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Generate C2_fixed256o32_hybrid:   0%|          | 0/100 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"5916653f5eca40b6a6edd5a341244e8c"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Generate C3_fixed256o32_hybrid_rerank:   0%|          | 0/100 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"1d039e4b6fc7472f8a6b73f38f58b62d"}},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"Final outputs: 300 | generation attempts including recoveries: 301\nstatus                        COMPLETED\ncondition                              \nC1_fixed128_bm25                    100\nC2_fixed256o32_hybrid               100\nC3_fixed256o32_hybrid_rerank        100\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":16},{"id":"cell-035","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 18. Claim extraction\n\nA response is split into sentence-like units. Only units containing at least four words are treated as evaluable claims, up to eight per answer. Abstentions, empty answers, malformed answers, and responses with no eligible claims are tracked separately and receive missing evidence-support scores rather than an artificial zero.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-036","cell_type":"code","source":"SENTENCE_SPLIT_RE = re.compile(r\"(?<=[.!?])\\s+|\\n+|(?<=;)\\s+\", re.UNICODE)\nWORD_RE = re.compile(r\"\\b[\\w'-]+\\b\", re.UNICODE)\n\ndef extract_claims(answer, max_claims=8, min_words=4):\n    claims = []\n    for candidate in SENTENCE_SPLIT_RE.split((answer or \"\").strip()):\n        claim = candidate.strip(\" \\t\\r\\n-*•\")\n        if len(WORD_RE.findall(claim)) >= min_words:\n            claims.append(claim)\n        if len(claims) >= max_claims:\n            break\n    return claims\n\nCLAIM_ROWS = []\nfor row in FINAL_OUTPUT_ROWS:\n    if row[\"status\"] != STATUS_COMPLETED or not row[\"answer_valid\"]:\n        continue\n    for index, claim in enumerate(extract_claims(row[\"answer\"], CFG[\"nli\"][\"max_claims_per_answer\"], CFG[\"nli\"][\"min_claim_words\"]), start=1):\n        CLAIM_ROWS.append({\"condition\": row[\"condition\"], \"query_id\": row[\"query_id\"], \"claim_index\": index,\n                           \"claim\": claim, \"claim_word_count\": len(WORD_RE.findall(claim))})\nCLAIMS = pd.DataFrame(CLAIM_ROWS)\nprint(\"Extracted evaluable claims:\", len(CLAIMS))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.657033Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.657392Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.676096Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.657368Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.675093Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Extracted evaluable claims: 344\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":17},{"id":"cell-037","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 19. Evidence-support assessment with NLI\n\nEach claim is evaluated as a hypothesis against up to five passages that were actually supplied to the generator, with each passage used as a premise. The maximum entailment probability over those passages is the claim-level support proxy; a claim is counted as supported when that probability is at least 0.50. NLI support is not proof of truth, completeness, source quality, or clinical correctness.\n\nThe label mapping is read from the model configuration. If the configuration uses generic `LABEL_0` names, the documented Sentence Transformers NLI order (contradiction, entailment, neutral) is used and explicitly recorded as a fallback.","metadata":{}},{"id":"cell-038","cell_type":"code","source":"from transformers import AutoModelForSequenceClassification\nNLI_TOKENIZER = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(MODEL_PATHS[\"nli\"], local_files_only=True)\nNLI_DEVICE = \"cuda:1\" if torch.cuda.device_count() >= 2 else GEN_DEVICE\nNLI_MODEL = AutoModelForSequenceClassification.from_pretrained(\n    MODEL_PATHS[\"nli\"], local_files_only=True,\n    use_safetensors=True if (Path(MODEL_PATHS[\"nli\"]) / \"model.safetensors\").exists() else False,\n).to(NLI_DEVICE).eval()\nraw_id2label = {int(k): str(v) for k, v in getattr(NLI_MODEL.config, \"id2label\", {}).items()}\nlabel_mapping_source = \"model_config_id2label\"\nnormalized_labels = {i: label.casefold().replace(\"_\", \" \") for i, label in raw_id2label.items()}\nentailment_ids = [i for i, label in normalized_labels.items() if \"entail\" in label]\nif len(entailment_ids) == 1:\n    NLI_ENTAILMENT_INDEX = entailment_ids[0]\nelse:\n    generic = all(label.startswith(\"label \") for label in normalized_labels.values())\n    if generic and len(normalized_labels) == 3:\n        # Sentence Transformers' documented model-card order for this NLI checkpoint.\n        NLI_LABEL_ORDER = [\"contradiction\", \"entailment\", \"neutral\"]\n        NLI_ENTAILMENT_INDEX = NLI_LABEL_ORDER.index(\"entailment\")\n        normalized_labels = {i: name for i, name in enumerate(NLI_LABEL_ORDER)}\n        label_mapping_source = \"Sentence-Transformers model documentation fallback for generic LABEL_n config\"\n    else:\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"Cannot identify a unique entailment label from model config: {raw_id2label}\")\n\nNLI_INFO = {\"repo_id\": MODEL_SPECS[\"nli\"][\"repo_id\"], \"commit_sha\": MODEL_REVISIONS[\"nli\"][\"resolved_commit_sha\"],\n            \"device\": NLI_DEVICE, \"id2label_raw\": raw_id2label, \"id2label_used\": normalized_labels,\n            \"entailment_index\": NLI_ENTAILMENT_INDEX, \"label_mapping_source\": label_mapping_source,\n            \"threshold\": CFG[\"nli\"][\"threshold\"], \"max_length\": CFG[\"nli\"][\"max_length\"]}\nsave_json(RES / \"nli_runtime.json\", NLI_INFO)\n\ndef nli_probabilities(premise_hypothesis_pairs, batch_size=16):\n    all_probs = []\n    for start in range(0, len(premise_hypothesis_pairs), batch_size):\n        batch = premise_hypothesis_pairs[start:start + batch_size]\n        premises = [p for p, h in batch]\n        hypotheses = [h for p, h in batch]\n        encoded = NLI_TOKENIZER(premises, hypotheses, padding=True, truncation=True,\n                                max_length=CFG[\"nli\"][\"max_length\"], return_tensors=\"pt\")\n        encoded = {k: v.to(NLI_DEVICE) for k, v in encoded.items()}\n        with torch.inference_mode():\n            logits = NLI_MODEL(**encoded).logits.float()\n        if logits.ndim != 2 or logits.shape[0] != len(batch) or logits.shape[1] != 3:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"Malformed NLI logits shape: {tuple(logits.shape)}\")\n        if not torch.isfinite(logits).all():\n            raise RuntimeError(\"NLI model returned NaN or infinite logits\")\n        probabilities = torch.softmax(logits, dim=-1).detach().cpu().numpy()\n        if not np.isfinite(probabilities).all():\n            raise RuntimeError(\"NLI softmax returned non-finite probabilities\")\n        all_probs.extend(probabilities.tolist())\n    return np.asarray(all_probs, dtype=float)\n\n# Diagnostic label sanity check; this does not tune the threshold or affect benchmark results.\nNLI_CALIBRATION_PAIRS = [\n    (\"The study enrolled 120 adults.\", \"The study included 120 adults.\"),\n    (\"The study enrolled 120 adults.\", \"The study enrolled 80 adults.\"),\n]\nNLI_CAL_PROBS = nli_probabilities(NLI_CALIBRATION_PAIRS)\nNLI_CAL_ROWS = []\nfor (premise, hypothesis), probs in zip(NLI_CALIBRATION_PAIRS, NLI_CAL_PROBS):\n    predicted_index = int(np.argmax(probs))\n    NLI_CAL_ROWS.append({\"premise\": premise, \"hypothesis\": hypothesis, \"predicted_label\": normalized_labels[predicted_index],\n                         \"entailment_probability\": float(probs[NLI_ENTAILMENT_INDEX]),\n                         \"contradiction_probability\": float(probs[[i for i, label in normalized_labels.items() if \"contradiction\" in label][0]]),\n                         \"diagnostic_only\": True})\nNLI_CAL_DF = pd.DataFrame(NLI_CAL_ROWS)\nNLI_CAL_DF.to_csv(RES / \"nli_calibration_controls.csv\", index=False)\ndisplay(NLI_CAL_DF)\n\nfaithfulness_rows = []\nfor row in tqdm(FINAL_OUTPUT_ROWS, desc=\"NLI evidence support\"):\n    if row[\"status\"] != STATUS_COMPLETED or not row[\"answer_valid\"]:\n        continue\n    evidence = row[\"evidence\"][:CFG[\"nli\"][\"max_passages_per_claim\"]]\n    claims = extract_claims(row[\"answer\"], CFG[\"nli\"][\"max_claims_per_answer\"], CFG[\"nli\"][\"min_claim_words\"])\n    if not claims or not evidence:\n        continue\n    pairs = [(item[\"text\"], claim) for claim in claims for item in evidence]\n    probabilities = nli_probabilities(pairs)\n    offset = 0\n    for claim_index, claim in enumerate(claims, start=1):\n        segment = probabilities[offset:offset + len(evidence)]\n        offset += len(evidence)\n        best_idx = int(np.argmax(segment[:, NLI_ENTAILMENT_INDEX]))\n        best_entailment = float(segment[best_idx, NLI_ENTAILMENT_INDEX])\n        faithfulness_rows.append({\n            \"condition\": row[\"condition\"], \"query_id\": row[\"query_id\"], \"claim_index\": claim_index,\n            \"claim\": claim, \"best_evidence_doc_id\": evidence[best_idx][\"doc_id\"],\n            \"best_evidence_chunk_id\": evidence[best_idx][\"chunk_id\"],\n            \"max_entailment_probability\": best_entailment,\n            \"supported\": bool(best_entailment >= CFG[\"nli\"][\"threshold\"]),\n            \"n_evidence_passages_compared\": len(evidence),\n        })\n\nFAITHFULNESS_CLAIMS = pd.DataFrame(faithfulness_rows, columns=[\n    \"condition\", \"query_id\", \"claim_index\", \"claim\", \"best_evidence_doc_id\", \"best_evidence_chunk_id\",\n    \"max_entailment_probability\", \"supported\", \"n_evidence_passages_compared\",\n])\nFAITHFULNESS_CLAIMS.to_csv(RES / \"faithfulness_claims.csv\", index=False)\nif len(FAITHFULNESS_CLAIMS):\n    FAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY = FAITHFULNESS_CLAIMS.groupby(\"condition\").agg(\n        evaluable_claims=(\"supported\", \"size\"), supported_claims=(\"supported\", \"sum\"),\n        mean_max_entailment=(\"max_entailment_probability\", \"mean\"),\n    ).reset_index()\n    FAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY[\"unsupported_claims\"] = FAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY[\"evaluable_claims\"] - FAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY[\"supported_claims\"]\n    FAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY[\"claim_level_support_rate\"] = FAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY[\"supported_claims\"] / FAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY[\"evaluable_claims\"]\nelse:\n    FAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY = pd.DataFrame(columns=[\"condition\", \"evaluable_claims\", \"supported_claims\", \"mean_max_entailment\", \"unsupported_claims\", \"claim_level_support_rate\"])\nFAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY.to_csv(RES / \"faithfulness_summary.csv\", index=False)\ndisplay(FAITHFULNESS_SUMMARY)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.677321Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.677861Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-03T07:23:12.688708Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-03T07:22:52.677837Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-03T07:23:12.687705Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"Loading weights:   0%|          | 0/202 [00:00<?, ?it/s]","application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json":{"version_major":2,"version_minor":0,"model_id":"7045910ff74b4865af47baa6590c978c"}},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"                          premise                      hypothesis  \\\n0  The study enrolled 120 adults.  The study included 120 adults.   \n1  The study enrolled 120 adults.   The study enrolled 80 adults.   \n\n  predicted_label  entailment_probability  contradiction_probability  \\\n0      entailment                0.998510                   0.000074   \n1   contradiction                0.000104                   0.999644   \n\n   diagnostic_only  \n0             True  \n1             True  ","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        te