ization to other biomedical collections is not established.\n- The dense encoder and reranker are general/MS MARCO models, not clinical decision systems. Their relevance scores are not clinical evidence.\n- A regex-based sentence splitter may mishandle abbreviations, dosage notation, and biomedical text fragments.\n- Exact dense search avoids approximate-index recall loss but does not represent every production ANN latency profile.\n- Reranking only examines the top 20 parent documents from a 100-document first-stage pool; it cannot recover candidates outside that pool.\n- NLI entailment, embedding similarity, cross-encoder query-answer score, and copying ratio are automatic proxies. No human clinical review or reference-answer accuracy is claimed.\n- A single seed/run does not estimate run-to-run variation. Paired bootstrap intervals quantify query-level variation within this evaluation set.\n- The historical manuscript's run produced empty generations and lacked recorded model revision hashes. All outputs in this notebook belong to a fresh, separately pinned run and must be interpreted from its own reports and manifest.","metadata":{}}]}